window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["story-v-y3v1-index"]=[{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p10-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami sakayanagi-arisu horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune prologue  the third year classroom and the class 3 a nameplate on the first day of class 3 a  horikita climbs to the third year floor before classes and stops before the newly polished  class 3 a  nameplate   i ve finally made it here   from class 1 d to class 3 a  she entered school only to follow after her older brother  who kept his distance at first  school life taught her that chasing him was not enough  and she came to understand his true feelings  she is on the student council and read a congratulatory speech at the entrance ceremony  she must not be complacent   if he hadn t been in the same class  i certainly wouldn t be who i am now  she set her sights on graduating from class a not just for her brother or herself  but to share the joy with everyone in the class  starting with ayanokoji  ryuen s class is catching up fast  ichinose s class and the former sakayanagi class must not be underestimated either   to think i d be next to him again  huh  her seat is the second row from the corridor  fourth from the front  next to it  first row  fourth seat  is ayanokoji kun s name   the same desk pairing as their first year  grateful  determined and privately anxious   resolves to graduate from class a with this class and these companions  and not to let it end as just a dream  attributes who she has become to his presence and is quietly delighted to be seated beside him again  the seating cheer is cut short by his unexplained absence later that morning  her older brother  unnamed in the text  the roster s horikita manabu  whom she followed into the school and whose distancing she first resented and later came to understand  notes his class is catching up quickly behind class a  acknowledges her class  like the former sakayanagi class  must not be underestimated  mentions the former sakayanagi class as a rival to watch","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p10-1\">Prologue: the third-year classroom and the Class 3-A nameplate<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.10–12<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the first day of Class 3-A, Horikita climbs to the third-year floor before classes and stops before the newly polished &quot;Class 3-A&quot; nameplate.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ve finally made it here…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;From Class 1-D to Class 3-A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She entered school only to follow after her older brother, who kept his distance at first; school life taught her that chasing him was not enough, and she came to understand his true feelings.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> She is on the student council and read a congratulatory speech at the entrance ceremony; she must not be complacent.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;If he hadn&#x27;t been in the same class, I certainly wouldn&#x27;t be who I am now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> She set her sights on graduating from Class A not just for her brother or herself, but to share the joy with everyone in the class, starting with Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Ryūen&#x27;s class is catching up fast; Ichinose&#x27;s class and the former Sakayanagi class must not be underestimated either.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;To think I&#x27;d be next to him again, huh…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Her seat is the second row from the corridor, fourth from the front; next to it (first row, fourth seat) is Ayanokōji-kun&#x27;s name — the same desk pairing as their first year.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Grateful, determined and privately anxious — resolves to graduate from Class A with this class and these companions, and not to let it end as just a dream.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Attributes who she has become to his presence and is quietly delighted to be seated beside him again; the seating cheer is cut short by his unexplained absence later that morning.<span class=\"pg\">p.11–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Her older brother (unnamed in the text; the roster&#x27;s horikita-manabu), whom she followed into the school and whose distancing she first resented and later came to understand.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Notes his class is catching up quickly behind Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Acknowledges her class, like the former Sakayanagi class, must not be underestimated.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Mentions the former Sakayanagi class as a rival to watch.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p13-1\">→ After: The transfer announcement shocks Class A<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p13-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the transfer announcement shocks class a notices ayanokoji absent on the first day of class 3 a  discusses with sudo whether he s feigning sickness over the karuizawa breakup   once is okay  but if it happens repeatedly  as a class  we can t just ignore it   sensei  are you alright   what are you talking about  something like ayanokouji kun transferring to class c  initially calm and analytical  but the transfer announcement shatters her composure   her voice trembles  her heart races  and she can t accept what the oaa confirms  deeply shaken by his unannounced transfer  refuses to believe it at first","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p13-1\">The transfer announcement shocks Class A<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.13–20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Notices Ayanokōji absent on the first day of Class 3-A; discusses with Sudō whether he&#x27;s feigning sickness over the Karuizawa breakup.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Once is okay. But if it happens repeatedly, as a class, we can&#x27;t just ignore it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Sensei, are you alright?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;What are you talking about…? Something like Ayanokouji-kun transferring to Class C…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Initially calm and analytical, but the transfer announcement shatters her composure — her voice trembles, her heart races, and she can&#x27;t accept what the OAA confirms.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Deeply shaken by his unannounced transfer; refuses to believe it at first.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p10-1\">← Before: Prologue: the third-year classroom and the Class 3-A nameplate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p24-1\">→ After: The class debates; Kushida and Hirata&#x27;s composure<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p13-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken sudo s theory  ayanokoji is dodging karuizawa  come to think of it  yeah   maybe he s pretending to be sick   he and karuizawa recently broke up  right  it must be pretty awkward to face each other   for me too  you know  when i experienced heartbreak  it really took a toll on me mentally   well  it s just a possibility  cut him some slack if he s a bit late  speaks from personal experience  he confessed to horikita on the school trip  suggests the breakup explains ayanokoji s absence  and urges giving him slack  later stands up when kushida needles horikita  sits diagonally behind her  worried about ayanokoji  recalls his own confession to her  speculates he s avoiding karuizawa after their breakup  notes she s been blatantly avoiding ayanokoji since morning","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p13-1\">Sudō&#x27;s theory: Ayanokōji is dodging Karuizawa<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.13–15<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Come to think of it, yeah.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Maybe he&#x27;s pretending to be sick.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;He and Karuizawa recently broke up, right? It must be pretty awkward to face each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;For me too, you know, when I experienced heartbreak, it really took a toll on me mentally.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, it&#x27;s just a possibility. Cut him some slack if he&#x27;s a bit late.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Speaks from personal experience (he confessed to Horikita on the school trip); suggests the breakup explains Ayanokōji&#x27;s absence, and urges giving him slack; later stands up when Kushida needles Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sits diagonally behind her, worried about Ayanokōji; recalls his own confession to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Speculates he&#x27;s avoiding Karuizawa after their breakup.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Notes she&#x27;s been blatantly avoiding Ayanokōji since morning.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p69-1\">→ After: Sudō demands answers from Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p14-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei karuizawa after the breakup  questioned about the transfer sits near the back by the window  listless  gazing outside  blatantly avoiding ayanokoji since morning   i don t know  i really don t know anything  it s not that i m hiding anything  i truly don t know  heartbroken after the breakup   listless and avoiding ayanokoji  when the class turns to her as his girlfriend  she says indifferently she knows nothing  her expression clouded also by guilt that the breakup caused his transfer  recently broke up with him  everyone assumes she might know why he transferred  but she doesn t  horikita senses her guilt and reads the room for her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p14-1\">Karuizawa after the breakup, questioned about the transfer<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.14–26<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits near the back by the window, listless, gazing outside; blatantly avoiding Ayanokōji since morning.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;…I don&#x27;t know. I really don&#x27;t know anything. It&#x27;s not that I&#x27;m hiding anything; I truly don&#x27;t know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Heartbroken after the breakup — listless and avoiding Ayanokōji; when the class turns to her as his girlfriend, she says indifferently she knows nothing, her expression clouded also by guilt that the breakup caused his transfer.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Recently broke up with him; everyone assumes she might know why he transferred, but she doesn&#x27;t.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita senses her guilt and reads the room for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p163-1\">→ After: Karuizawa&#x27;s heartbreak; confronting Ichinose about Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p16-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira announces the transfer  ends the homeroom with a warning arrives pale with unfocused  lifeless eyes and does not respond to hirata or kikuchi  after a long silence she murmurs that she is fine   i m fine   there s something i need to tell all of you  this morning no  just a little while ago a certain student used their private points to exercise a certain right  or so it seems   the student who s absent from the classroom right now  ayanokouji  he s the one who exercised that right   class  transfer   i understand that what i m saying is hard to grasp  however  it s the truth   take out your phone and display the class oaa   ayanokouji has been transferred from this class to class c as of today  asked whether an illegal transfer could be canceled  the answer   that an illegal transfer could be canceled but the fraud committer would face severe punishment and  the arrows would also point at ayanokouji    is not speaker tagged in the translation  on subject matter it reads as chabashira s  but the attribution is not printed   y yes  that s right   let s end the homeroom period here  however  i ask that you don t take action against ayanokouji for the sake of blaming or criticizing him  currently  he hasn t done anything against the rules   that s right  avoid unnecessary contact with ayanokouji  and make sure not to get into trouble with other classes  if anything happens  make sure to go through me or the school  okay  uncharacteristically shattered   keeps glancing at her tablet and cannot give a straight explanation  students later realize how much they did not know about his standing in the class  delivers the news of his transfer  instructs the class not to blame or contact him  for rules and safety reasons  first to ask after her  he then echoes her warning about avoiding unnecessary contact  she signals to end the homeroom  chabashira agrees aloud  the print run leaves these pages without prose  blank","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p16-1\">Chabashira announces the transfer; ends the homeroom with a warning<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.16–28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives pale with unfocused, lifeless eyes and does not respond to Hirata or Kikuchi; after a long silence she murmurs that she is fine.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;There&#x27;s something I need to tell all of you. This morning—no, just a little while ago—a certain student used their Private Points to exercise a certain right… or so it seems.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;The student who&#x27;s absent from the classroom right now… Ayanokouji. He&#x27;s the one who exercised that right.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…Class… transfer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I understand that what I&#x27;m saying is hard to grasp. However… it&#x27;s the truth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Take out your phone and display the class OAA.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji has been transferred from this class to Class C as of today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asked whether an illegal transfer could be canceled, the answer — that an illegal transfer could be canceled but the fraud-committer would face severe punishment and &quot;the arrows would also point at Ayanokouji&quot; — is not speaker-tagged in the translation; on subject matter it reads as Chabashira&#x27;s, but the attribution is not printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…Y-Yes, that&#x27;s right.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s end the homeroom period here. However, I ask that you don&#x27;t take action against Ayanokouji for the sake of blaming or criticizing him. Currently, he hasn&#x27;t done anything against the rules.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s right. Avoid unnecessary contact with Ayanokouji, and make sure not to get into trouble with other classes. If anything happens, make sure to go through me or the school, okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Uncharacteristically shattered — keeps glancing at her tablet and cannot give a straight explanation; students later realize how much they did not know about his standing in the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Delivers the news of his transfer; instructs the class not to blame or contact him, for rules and safety reasons.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> First to ask after her; he then echoes her warning about avoiding unnecessary contact.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She signals to end the homeroom; Chabashira agrees aloud.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The print run leaves these pages without prose (blank).<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p87-1\">→ After: Chabashira tails Ayanokōji; asks whether the transfer was on her account<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p16-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune chabashira-sae hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke hirata checks on chabashira  urges accepting reality  sensei  are you alright   you say that  but you clearly seem unwell   i think we should start by accepting reality   just what it sounds like  he  ayanokouji kun  has transferred classes   transfer and expulsion are different  especially if it s his own decision   i agree with chabashira sensei  not only from a rules perspective  but also because approaching him in large numbers without understanding the situation can easily lead to trouble  i ll check on things first  the first to check on the dazed chabashira  and the calmest student after the announcement   urges accepting the confirmed reality  refuses to panic  and takes charge of investigating to keep the class from acting rashly  uncharacteristically composed  which kushida notes  tries to reach the flustered horikita  she can t match his calm  first to notice and check on her unwell state","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p16-1\">Hirata checks on Chabashira; urges accepting reality<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.16–28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;Sensei, are you alright?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;You say that, but you clearly seem unwell.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;I think we should start by accepting reality.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just what it sounds like. He, Ayanokouji-kun, has transferred classes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Transfer and expulsion are different. Especially if it&#x27;s his own decision.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I agree with Chabashira-sensei. Not only from a rules perspective, but also because approaching him in large numbers without understanding the situation can easily lead to trouble. I&#x27;ll check on things first.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The first to check on the dazed Chabashira, and the calmest student after the announcement — urges accepting the confirmed reality, refuses to panic, and takes charge of investigating to keep the class from acting rashly (uncharacteristically composed, which Kushida notes).<span class=\"pg\">p.16–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Tries to reach the flustered Horikita; she can&#x27;t match his calm.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> First to notice and check on her unwell state.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p66-1\">→ After: Hirata&#x27;s private talk and respectful acceptance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kikuchi-y3v1-p16-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae kikuchi","q":"kikuchi kikuchi waves at the unresponsive chabashira from the front seat closest to chabashira  calls out tentatively  when she does not respond  stands and waves a hand in front of her face  which finally draws her glance   um  sensei  the class grows anxious at chabashira s unresponsiveness  kikuchi s gesture is the only thing that briefly registers with her  tries to get her attention  she only registers them in passing before her gaze settles on horikita s direction","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kikuchi-y3v1-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kikuchi waves at the unresponsive Chabashira<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.16<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kikuchi\">Kikuchi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">From the front seat closest to Chabashira, calls out tentatively; when she does not respond, stands and waves a hand in front of her face, which finally draws her glance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kikuchi<\/b> &quot;Um… Sensei?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The class grows anxious at Chabashira&#x27;s unresponsiveness; Kikuchi&#x27;s gesture is the only thing that briefly registers with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Tries to get her attention; she only registers them in passing before her gaze settles on Horikita&#x27;s direction.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y3v1-p20-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae matsushita-chiaki","q":"matsushita chiaki matsushita  flustered at the announcement raises her voice in a way unlike her  some students cannot hide their surprise at the unusual behavior   t this is a lie  right  sensei  that ayanokouji kun has transferred to class c  demands confirmation  chabashira holds that it is not a mistake","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y3v1-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html#sc-matsushita-chiaki-y3v1-p20-1\">Matsushita, flustered at the announcement<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.20–21<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Raises her voice in a way unlike her; some students cannot hide their surprise at the unusual behavior.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> &quot;T-This is a lie, right, Sensei? That Ayanokouji-kun has transferred to Class C…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Demands confirmation; Chabashira holds that it is not a mistake.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y3v1-p30-1\">→ After: Matsushita accompanies Horikita; Ayanokōji exposes their partnership<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y3v1-p24-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"","w":"shinohara-satsuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka hondou-ryoutaro","q":"hondo ryotaro hondou responds in kind reacts to shinohara s doubts with a similar suspicion amid the class s speculation over the transfer  the unattributed lines in this exchange include  or is that what this is about  and  could he have betrayed us  the narration says hondou responded to shinohara with a similar suspicion  without pinning lines to speakers  echoes her speculation  shares the sense that the transfer is  just not normal  while sakayanagi s departure makes it hard to read","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y3v1-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hondou-ryoutaro.html#sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y3v1-p24-1\">Hondou responds in kind<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.24<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hondou-ryoutaro.html\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reacts to Shinohara&#x27;s doubts with a similar suspicion amid the class&#x27;s speculation over the transfer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The unattributed lines in this exchange include &quot;Or is that what this is about?&quot; and &quot;Could he have betrayed us?&quot;; the narration says Hondou responded to Shinohara with a similar suspicion, without pinning lines to speakers.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Echoes her speculation.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Shares the sense that the transfer is &quot;just not normal,&quot; while Sakayanagi&#x27;s departure makes it hard to read.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p24-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the class debates  kushida and hirata s composure  yes  setting aside ayanokouji kun s intentions  there s no denying he s the ideal recruit for class c s comeback   but that s  that s not proof  he might just be sick  or it could be some sort of a mistake  clings to the hope of a mistake  notes chabashira s shock proves ayanokoji was too important to lose  rattled by kushida s pointed questions and hirata s calm acceptance  kushida passes her the question of ayanokoji s importance  later needles hirata s uncharacteristic calm  he urges accepting reality  she can t match his composure","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p24-1\">The class debates; Kushida and Hirata&#x27;s composure<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.24–28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Yes… Setting aside Ayanokouji-kun&#x27;s intentions, there&#x27;s no denying he&#x27;s the ideal recruit for Class C&#x27;s comeback.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;But that&#x27;s… that&#x27;s not proof. He might just be sick, or it could be some sort of a mistake…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Clings to the hope of a mistake; notes Chabashira&#x27;s shock proves Ayanokōji was too important to lose; rattled by Kushida&#x27;s pointed questions and Hirata&#x27;s calm acceptance.<span class=\"pg\">p.24–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida passes her the question of Ayanokōji&#x27;s importance; later needles Hirata&#x27;s uncharacteristic calm.<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He urges accepting reality; she can&#x27;t match his composure.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p13-1\">← Before: The transfer announcement shocks Class A<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p29-1\">→ After: Rushing to confront Ayanokōji; self-doubt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-miyake-akito-y3v1-p24-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko miyake-akito","q":"miyake akito akito  not a word beforehand classmates ask ayanokoji s inner circle whether they knew anything  akito answers from the bench   no  not a word  we ve been a bit distant lately  if even horikita and the others don t know  then probably no one does  the question  did you hear anything beforehand  akito  is untagged in the translation  the reply is akito s by name  he and yukimura are named as the circle ayanokoji was closest to  all unaware of the transfer  named beside him as inner circle  equally uninformed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-miyake-akito-y3v1-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html#sc-miyake-akito-y3v1-p24-1\">Akito: not a word beforehand<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.24<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classmates ask Ayanokōji&#x27;s inner circle whether they knew anything; Akito answers from the bench.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> &quot;No, not a word… We&#x27;ve been a bit distant lately. If even Horikita and the others don&#x27;t know, then probably no one does.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question &quot;Did you hear anything beforehand, Akito?&quot; is untagged in the translation; the reply is Akito&#x27;s by name. He and Yukimura are named as the circle Ayanokōji was closest to, all unaware of the transfer.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Named beside him as inner-circle, equally uninformed.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-miyake-akito-y3v1-p70-1\">→ After: Akito asks, then offers friendship<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y3v1-p24-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"","w":"hondou-ryoutaro ayanokouji-kiyotaka shinohara-satsuki","q":"shinohara satsuki shinohara mutters her doubts among the class 3 a students speculating about the transfer after the oaa confirms it  the translation leaves the speculation lines in this stretch unattributed  the narration says shinohara muttered her doubts  to which hondou responded with a similar suspicion  lines such as  could he have betrayed us  and  or is that what this is about  cannot be assigned to her with certainty  echo each other s suspicions  the text does not pin specific lines to either of them  considers with hondou whether he might have betrayed the class  though the transfer makes little sense to them  it s not like he s jumping on the winning horse","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y3v1-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html#sc-shinohara-satsuki-y3v1-p24-1\">Shinohara mutters her doubts<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.24<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Among the Class 3-A students speculating about the transfer after the OAA confirms it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hondou-ryoutaro.html\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves the speculation lines in this stretch unattributed; the narration says Shinohara muttered her doubts, to which Hondou responded with a similar suspicion. Lines such as &quot;Could he have betrayed us?&quot; and &quot;Or is that what this is about?&quot; cannot be assigned to her with certainty.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/b> Echo each other&#x27;s suspicions; the text does not pin specific lines to either of them.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Considers with Hondou whether he might have betrayed the class, though the transfer makes little sense to them (&quot;It&#x27;s not like he&#x27;s jumping on the winning horse&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p25-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke ike-kanji kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo kushida  ayanokoji was more important than assumed  that s a possibility   ike kun  shinohara san  sorry  but ayanokouji kun is much more important than you two think   just because it hasn t come to light doesn t mean he hasn t contributed to the class in countless unseen ways   you seem quite calm  hirata kun  whether it s a transfer or expulsion  a student may have disappeared from our class  and yet you re not disturbed  calm amidst the chaos and aware of ayanokoji s hidden contributions  pointedly questions hirata s uncharacteristic composure and pushes to end the homeroom discussion before eavesdroppers overhear  recognizes his unseen contributions to the class  needles him for being too calm about the disappearance  criticizes him and shinohara for underestimating ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p25-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p25-1\">Kushida: Ayanokōji was more important than assumed<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.25–28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;That&#x27;s a possibility.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Ike-kun, Shinohara-san, sorry, but Ayanokouji-kun is much more important than you two think.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Just because it hasn&#x27;t come to light doesn&#x27;t mean he hasn&#x27;t contributed to the class in countless unseen ways.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You seem quite calm, Hirata-kun. Whether it&#x27;s a transfer or expulsion, a student may have disappeared from our class, and yet you&#x27;re not disturbed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm amidst the chaos and aware of Ayanokōji&#x27;s hidden contributions; pointedly questions Hirata&#x27;s uncharacteristic composure and pushes to end the homeroom discussion before eavesdroppers overhear.<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Recognizes his unseen contributions to the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Needles him for being too calm about the disappearance.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Criticizes him and Shinohara for underestimating Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p126-1\">→ After: Kushida needles the gloomy Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p29-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune rushing to confront ayanokoji  self doubt after school  resolves to confirm ayanokoji s true intentions  trembling at the thought of seeing him   i wanted to see him   i didn t want to see him   honestly  i did feel a bit scared about seeing him   that was a lie  i was very scared   ayanokouji kun  why   am i really that unreliable  tortured by indecision and fear  then bitter self doubt   wonders if she seemed like a child to him  unworthy of being relied upon  resolves to save him if the transfer wasn t his will  he tries to speak  she brushes him off to go meet ayanokoji  desperate to hear his intentions from his own lips before deciding anything","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p29-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p29-1\">Rushing to confront Ayanokōji; self-doubt<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.29–33<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After school, resolves to confirm Ayanokōji&#x27;s true intentions, trembling at the thought of seeing him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I wanted to see him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I didn&#x27;t want to see him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Honestly, I did feel a bit scared about seeing him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;That was a lie. I was very scared.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun… Why…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;…Am I really that unreliable?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Tortured by indecision and fear, then bitter self-doubt — wonders if she seemed like a child to him, unworthy of being relied upon; resolves to save him if the transfer wasn&#x27;t his will.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He tries to speak; she brushes him off to go meet Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Desperate to hear his intentions from his own lips before deciding anything.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p24-1\">← Before: The class debates; Kushida and Hirata&#x27;s composure<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p34-1\">→ After: The café confrontation; Ayanokōji&#x27;s cold exposure<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y3v1-p30-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune matsushita-chiaki","q":"matsushita chiaki matsushita accompanies horikita  ayanokoji exposes their partnership  i know  you re going to see ayanokouji kun  right  let me come with you   i want to know the reason behind ayanokouji kun s transfer  just to confirm once more  this isn t part of your strategy  horikita san  right   i m just accompanying her  i m only here to convey to my class what i ve seen and heard as a normal classmate rather than a leader   oh no  ayanokouji kun  you really seem to be overestimating me  a  schemer  who values ayanokoji s abilities   accompanies horikita under the pretext of reporting to her class  but ayanokoji reveals she came to verify his true intentions and that she had cooperated with him behind the scenes  including maezono s expulsion  she can t fully hide her disturbance at the exposure  secretly cooperated with him  came to verify his reasons for transferring  accompanies her  claiming to be a neutral classmate reporter  ayanokoji calls her  one of the sharpest minds in horikita s class  usually working behind the scenes   you re okay with not answering anything  ayanokouji kun  you ll be treated as a traitor  you know  her persistence produces the only answer he gives   that there is nothing more to say  horikita gives up and leaves","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y3v1-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html#sc-matsushita-chiaki-y3v1-p30-1\">Matsushita accompanies Horikita; Ayanokōji exposes their partnership<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.30–39<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> &quot;I know. You&#x27;re going to see Ayanokouji-kun, right? Let me come with you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> &quot;…I want to know the reason behind Ayanokouji-kun&#x27;s transfer. Just to confirm once more, this isn&#x27;t part of your strategy, Horikita-san, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m just accompanying her. I&#x27;m only here to convey to my class what I&#x27;ve seen and heard as a normal classmate rather than a leader.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh no, Ayanokouji-kun, you really seem to be overestimating me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> A &quot;schemer&quot; who values Ayanokōji&#x27;s abilities — accompanies Horikita under the pretext of reporting to her class, but Ayanokōji reveals she came to verify his true intentions and that she had cooperated with him behind the scenes (including Maezono&#x27;s expulsion); she can&#x27;t fully hide her disturbance at the exposure.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> secretly cooperated with him; came to verify his reasons for transferring.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Accompanies her, claiming to be a neutral classmate reporter.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji calls her &quot;one of the sharpest minds in Horikita&#x27;s class,&quot; usually working behind the scenes.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re okay with not answering anything? Ayanokouji-kun, you&#x27;ll be treated as a traitor, you know?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her persistence produces the only answer he gives — that there is nothing more to say; Horikita gives up and leaves.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y3v1-p20-1\">← Before: Matsushita, flustered at the announcement<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p34-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune matsushita-chiaki hashimoto-masayoshi ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ayanokoji at the cafe  coldly cutting ties with class a sits in the keyaki mall cafe with hashimoto  morishita and ichinose  conversing indifferently an hour after the transfer   i won t deny it  with sakayanagi around  that chance was nonexistent anyway   what matsushita just mentioned about being an accompaniment must be a pretext   but in reality  she s quite a schemer   there have been several instances where you ve skillfully arranged things from behind the scenes when i needed help   there s no point in exploring the reasons for the transfer  i haven t told anyone about this  not horikita  not matsushita not anyone in the class   it s scary when a student leaves the class  huh  horikita  deliberately cold   refuses to explain  reveals he told no one in class a  and casually exposes his secret cooperation with matsushita  including maezono s expulsion  making it clear he is no longer their ally and shifting the ground to class c s advantage  blocks her questions  exposes matsushita to rattle her  and tells her there s no point exploring the transfer s reasons  reveals their behind the scenes cooperation  praising her as  one of the sharpest minds in horikita s class  lets him act as gatekeeper  chuckles at his  leader candidate  claim  present at the cafe  she listens with keen interest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p34-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p34-1\">Ayanokōji at the café: coldly cutting ties with Class A<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.34–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits in the Keyaki Mall café with Hashimoto, Morishita and Ichinose, conversing indifferently an hour after the transfer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I won&#x27;t deny it. With Sakayanagi around, that chance was nonexistent anyway.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;What Matsushita just mentioned about being an accompaniment must be a pretext.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;But in reality, she&#x27;s quite a schemer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There have been several instances where you&#x27;ve skillfully arranged things from behind the scenes when I needed help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s no point in exploring the reasons for the transfer. I haven&#x27;t told anyone about this, not Horikita, not Matsushita—not anyone in the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s scary when a student leaves the class, huh, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately cold — refuses to explain, reveals he told no one in Class A, and casually exposes his secret cooperation with Matsushita (including Maezono&#x27;s expulsion), making it clear he is no longer their ally and shifting the ground to Class C&#x27;s advantage.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Blocks her questions, exposes Matsushita to rattle her, and tells her there&#x27;s no point exploring the transfer&#x27;s reasons.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Reveals their behind-the-scenes cooperation, praising her as &quot;one of the sharpest minds in Horikita&#x27;s class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Lets him act as gatekeeper; chuckles at his &quot;leader candidate&quot; claim.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Present at the café; she listens with keen interest.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-1\">→ After: Arriving in Class C; Morishita seats him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v1-p34-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi hashimoto the gatekeeper  hey  horikita  we re in the middle of a strategy meeting right now  but do you need something   if you want to talk to our leader candidate  you ll have to go through me first   it s not sudden  i ve been waiting for this moment all along  right  ayanokouji   i see  as the class leader  huh  well  it s certainly natural since a classmate suddenly left  but that makes it all the more reason why i can t let you check  it s convenient for us if you guys are troubled   don t glare at me like that  by the way  why s matsushita here at this crucial moment  sly and opportunistic   blocks horikita from reaching ayanokoji  calls him the  leader candidate  openly enjoys class a s trouble  and pokes into why matsushita came  supports him as class c s leader candidate  acts as gatekeeper  denying her access","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v1-p34-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v1-p34-1\">Hashimoto the gatekeeper<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.34–35<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Hey, Horikita. We&#x27;re in the middle of a strategy meeting right now, but do you need something?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;If you want to talk to our leader candidate, you&#x27;ll have to go through me first.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s not sudden. I&#x27;ve been waiting for this moment all along. Right, Ayanokouji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see, as the class leader, huh? Well, it&#x27;s certainly natural since a classmate suddenly left, but that makes it all the more reason why I can&#x27;t let you check. It&#x27;s convenient for us if you guys are troubled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don&#x27;t glare at me like that. By the way, why&#x27;s Matsushita here at this crucial moment?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sly and opportunistic — blocks Horikita from reaching Ayanokōji, calls him the &quot;leader candidate,&quot; openly enjoys Class A&#x27;s trouble, and pokes into why Matsushita came.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Supports him as Class C&#x27;s leader candidate.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Acts as gatekeeper, denying her access.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v1-p45-1\">→ After: The welcome party and the money talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p34-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hashimoto-masayoshi matsushita-chiaki ichinose-honami horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the cafe confrontation  ayanokoji s cold exposure arrives at the keyaki mall cafe with matsushita  finds ayanokoji with hashimoto  morishita and ichinose  conversing indifferently   i want you to let me have a conversation with ayanokouji kun   leader candidate  that s quite a sudden thing to say   sorry  but i need you to be quiet right now  hashimoto kun  as the class leader  i have to grasp the current situation   i see  indeed  it must look like a strange transfer to everyone but a few students  tries to stay calm and assert her role as leader  but is repeatedly blocked by hashimoto and stunned as ayanokoji coldly exposes matsushita s behind the scenes cooperation   realizing the ground has shifted to the opponent s territory  confronts him  he refuses to explain  reveals he told no one in class a  and casually exposes his secret partnership with matsushita   making clear he is no longer an ally  blocks her from reaching ayanokoji as his  leader candidate  gatekeeper  accompanies her  ayanokoji reveals matsushita was one of his behind the scenes collaborators  even with maezono s expulsion  shaking horikita  watches keenly  says she has much to learn about the students and will pay close attention to matsushita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p34-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p34-1\">The café confrontation; Ayanokōji&#x27;s cold exposure<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.34–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives at the Keyaki Mall café with Matsushita; finds Ayanokōji with Hashimoto, Morishita and Ichinose, conversing indifferently.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I want you to let me have a conversation with Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;…Leader candidate… That&#x27;s quite a sudden thing to say.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Sorry, but I need you to be quiet right now, Hashimoto-kun. As the class leader, I have to grasp the current situation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. Indeed, it must look like a strange transfer to everyone but a few students.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Tries to stay calm and assert her role as leader, but is repeatedly blocked by Hashimoto and stunned as Ayanokōji coldly exposes Matsushita&#x27;s behind-the-scenes cooperation — realizing the ground has shifted to the opponent&#x27;s territory.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Confronts him; he refuses to explain, reveals he told no one in Class A, and casually exposes his secret partnership with Matsushita — making clear he is no longer an ally.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Blocks her from reaching Ayanokōji as his &quot;leader candidate&quot; gatekeeper.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Accompanies her; Ayanokōji reveals Matsushita was one of his behind-the-scenes collaborators (even with Maezono&#x27;s expulsion), shaking Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Watches keenly; says she has much to learn about the students and will pay close attention to Matsushita.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p29-1\">← Before: Rushing to confront Ayanokōji; self-doubt<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p98-1\">→ After: A week on: grief, the exam announcement, and self-loathing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p37-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"matsushita-chiaki ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ichinose watches the confrontation with keen interest  i didn t know she was such a reliable person  i still have much to learn about the students here  from now on  i ll have to pay close attention to matsushita san  resting her chin on her hands and smiling  she absorbs the exchange   surprises horikita by already recognizing matsushita s reliability and resolves to watch her closely  impressed by her  decides to pay close attention to her  present at the cafe with him  listens keenly to the confrontation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p37-1\">Ichinose watches the confrontation with keen interest<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.37<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;I didn&#x27;t know she was such a reliable person. I still have much to learn about the students here. From now on, I&#x27;ll have to pay close attention to Matsushita-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Resting her chin on her hands and smiling, she absorbs the exchange — surprises Horikita by already recognizing Matsushita&#x27;s reliability and resolves to watch her closely.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Impressed by her; decides to pay close attention to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Present at the café with him; listens keenly to the confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p55-1\">→ After: Ichinose at the café: the alliance explained and defended<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"morishita-ai hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka arriving in class c  morishita seats him after submitting his transfer notice to the chairman  stands before class c and introduces himself   the opening ceremony just ended  but i  ayanokouji kiyotaka  have transferred to this class using twenty million private points   i can t replace sakayanagi  who voluntarily withdrew  but if there s still a will to fight among everyone here  i m confident that i can help overcome the class s greatly deteriorated situation  hashimoto   the biggest investor in his transfer   applauds first   glad to have ya  ayanokouji  most others watch with cold  skeptical gazes  which he judges is a sign of the class s quality  morishita proposes he sit in front of her  center ish  easily surveilled  not the coveted back window seat  sugio eagerly gives it up   about what s to come  carefully chooses his words  reflecting on his failed first year self introduction  reads the class as high quality but cautious and easy to navigate  she arranges his seat in front of her and peppers him with jokes  making 100 friends  eating onigiri with 100 people    classic references he doesn t know  the transfer s biggest investor  publicly welcomes him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-1\">Arriving in Class C; Morishita seats him<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.40–44<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After submitting his transfer notice to the chairman, stands before Class C and introduces himself.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;The opening ceremony just ended, but I, Ayanokouji Kiyotaka, have transferred to this class using twenty million Private Points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I can&#x27;t replace Sakayanagi, who voluntarily withdrew, but if there&#x27;s still a will to fight among everyone here, I&#x27;m confident that I can help overcome the class&#x27;s greatly deteriorated situation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;About what&#x27;s to come.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Hashimoto — the biggest investor in his transfer — applauds first: &quot;Glad to have ya, Ayanokouji&quot;; most others watch with cold, skeptical gazes, which he judges is a sign of the class&#x27;s quality.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Morishita proposes he sit in front of her (center-ish, easily surveilled, not the coveted back window seat); Sugio eagerly gives it up.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Carefully chooses his words, reflecting on his failed first-year self-introduction; reads the class as high-quality but cautious and easy to navigate.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> She arranges his seat in front of her and peppers him with jokes (making 100 friends, eating onigiri with 100 people) — classic references he doesn&#x27;t know.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> The transfer&#x27;s biggest investor; publicly welcomes him.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p34-1\">← Before: Ayanokōji at the café: coldly cutting ties with Class A<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p45-1\">→ After: The rejected welcome party<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p41-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hashimoto-masayoshi ichinose-honami morishita-ai","q":"morishita ai morishita seats  needles and vets ayanokoji  first  ayanokouji kiyotaka is like a transfer student  meaning he is new to the class and unfamiliar with it   moreover  since he s an unexpected foreign element from an opposing class  who was an enemy until recently  proper surveillance is necessary   it ll be a pleasure going forward  ayanokouji kiyotaka   wondering if you can make a hundred friends   ayanokouji kiyotaka  you re spectacularly unpopular  it s like you re leftover merchandise   i refuse    to the welcome party  are you serious  i mean  the arrangement is easy to understand  but what i want to point out is that there s no point in an alliance where victories are conceded   a tightly bound contract can sometimes be a fatal blow   can you unconditionally entrust an unknown student to create a strategy for the special exam  eccentric and sharp   arranges his seating under the pretext of surveillance  delivers odd onigiri make 100 friends jokes  bluntly calls him unpopular  refuses the party  then sharply vets the alliance  conceding victories wastes opportunities  and points out hashimoto would oppose the plan if he weren t invested  seats him  needles him  follows him to vet the alliance  one of the few who was informed in advance  points out that if hashimoto hadn t brought ayanokoji in  he d be the prime candidate for opposing him  doubts the  good natured  class d leader  attends to verify whether collaborating makes sense","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p41-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html#sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p41-1\">Morishita seats, needles and vets Ayanokōji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.41–68<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;First, Ayanokouji Kiyotaka is like a transfer student, meaning he is new to the class and unfamiliar with it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;Moreover, since he&#x27;s an unexpected foreign element from an opposing class, who was an enemy until recently, proper surveillance is necessary.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;ll be a pleasure going forward, Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Wondering if you can make a hundred friends?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji Kiyotaka, you&#x27;re spectacularly unpopular. It&#x27;s like you&#x27;re leftover merchandise.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I refuse.&quot; — to the welcome party<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Are you serious? I mean, the arrangement is easy to understand, but what I want to point out is that there&#x27;s no point in an alliance where victories are conceded.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A tightly bound contract can sometimes be a fatal blow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Can you unconditionally entrust an unknown student to create a strategy for the special exam?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Eccentric and sharp — arranges his seating under the pretext of surveillance, delivers odd onigiri/make-100-friends jokes, bluntly calls him unpopular, refuses the party, then sharply vets the alliance (conceding victories wastes opportunities) and points out Hashimoto would oppose the plan if he weren&#x27;t invested.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Seats him, needles him, follows him to vet the alliance; one of the few who was informed in advance.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Points out that if Hashimoto hadn&#x27;t brought Ayanokōji in, he&#x27;d be the prime candidate for opposing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Doubts the &quot;good-natured&quot; Class D leader; attends to verify whether collaborating makes sense.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p146-1\">→ After: Morishita&#x27;s eraser-crumb prank and &quot;Jeanne d&#x27;Arc&quot; defense<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p45-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the rejected welcome party hashimoto proposes a flashy welcome party at keyaki mall  the room goes tense   it s natural that they can t welcome me wholeheartedly   well  maybe  sits as a bystander  unable to ask for or refuse the party  notes the awkwardness is about him  and accepts morishita s blunt observation that he is  spectacularly unpopular  tries to throw him a welcome party  yoshida  machida and others refuse  saying he must prove his worth first  tells him he is  leftover merchandise  unpopular  and that if ichinose or kushida had transferred they d be surrounded by smiles","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p45-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p45-1\">The rejected welcome party<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.45–48<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hashimoto proposes a flashy welcome party at Keyaki Mall; the room goes tense.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s natural that they can&#x27;t welcome me wholeheartedly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;…Well… maybe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sits as a bystander, unable to ask for or refuse the party; notes the awkwardness is about him, and accepts Morishita&#x27;s blunt observation that he is &quot;spectacularly unpopular.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45–48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Tries to throw him a welcome party; Yoshida, Machida and others refuse, saying he must prove his worth first.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Tells him he is &quot;leftover merchandise,&quot; unpopular, and that if Ichinose or Kushida had transferred they&#x27;d be surrounded by smiles.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-1\">← Before: Arriving in Class C; Morishita seats him<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p49-1\">→ After: The contract with Hashimoto; reason for transferring via Class A money<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v1-p45-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yoshida-kenta hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi the welcome party and the money talk  kay  so  how about we all throw a welcome party for ayanokouji at keyaki mall and make it flashy   man  your boldness is something else  i never imagined you d plan to transfer to our class  and to think you used my money for it   in these past two years  i ve crossed many dangerous bridges on my own   it s fine to trust you on that  right  ayanokouji  that from here on  you ll seriously aim for class a   hey  stop with the bad jokes  ayanokouji  i m all in on you  literally penniless  the transfer s biggest investor   proposes the welcome party  repeatedly complains about the 20 million but accepted the risk  insisting he s fully committed and  penniless  calls ayanokoji s betrayal joke unfunny  invested the transfer money  committed to him despite the cost  his welcome party proposal is refused by yoshida and others","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v1-p45-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v1-p45-1\">The welcome party and the money talk<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.45–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Kay. So, how about we all throw a welcome party for Ayanokouji at Keyaki Mall and make it flashy?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Man, your boldness is something else… I never imagined you&#x27;d plan to transfer to our class. And to think you used my money for it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;In these past two years, I&#x27;ve crossed many dangerous bridges on my own.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s fine to trust you on that, right, Ayanokouji? That from here on, you&#x27;ll seriously aim for Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hey, stop with the bad jokes, Ayanokouji. I&#x27;m all in on you, literally penniless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The transfer&#x27;s biggest investor — proposes the welcome party, repeatedly complains about the 20 million but accepted the risk, insisting he&#x27;s fully committed and &quot;penniless&quot;; calls Ayanokōji&#x27;s betrayal joke unfunny.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Invested the transfer money; committed to him despite the cost.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> His welcome-party proposal is refused by Yoshida and others.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v1-p34-1\">← Before: Hashimoto the gatekeeper<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p49-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the contract with hashimoto  reason for transferring via class a money  it s only a matter of time   i told you when we talked about the transfer  i won t guarantee anything when making decisions   i m worried about being betrayed like sakayanagi   for this transfer  class c s unanimous consent was a must  there were things i couldn t entrust to you and your problematic issues  he gave hashimoto a choice  give up his fortune and accept him  or forgo accepting him entirely   knowing hashimoto s sunk cost investment and risky position made accepting the only rational choice  coldly strategic   keeps hashimoto slightly tense  withholds strategy  and brought morishita in because her doubts forced him to share information hashimoto couldn t be trusted with  discusses the transfer  the money  and his risks  hashimoto insists he s  all in  penniless  she followed them  calls him the  embodiment of unpopularity  and attacks on  presence popularity  wordplay  she joins to verify the alliance with ichinose","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p49-1\">The contract with Hashimoto; reason for transferring via Class A money<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.49–54<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s only a matter of time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I told you when we talked about the transfer. I won&#x27;t guarantee anything when making decisions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m worried about being betrayed like Sakayanagi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;For this transfer, Class C&#x27;s unanimous consent was a must. There were things I couldn&#x27;t entrust to you and your problematic issues.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> He gave Hashimoto a choice: give up his fortune and accept him, or forgo accepting him entirely — knowing Hashimoto&#x27;s sunk-cost investment and risky position made accepting the only rational choice.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coldly strategic — keeps Hashimoto slightly tense, withholds strategy, and brought Morishita in because her doubts forced him to share information Hashimoto couldn&#x27;t be trusted with.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Discusses the transfer, the money, and his risks; Hashimoto insists he&#x27;s &quot;all in... penniless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> She followed them, calls him the &quot;embodiment of unpopularity&quot; and attacks on &quot;presence&quot;/&quot;popularity&quot; wordplay; she joins to verify the alliance with Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p45-1\">← Before: The rejected welcome party<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p55-1\">→ After: The café: explaining the alliance; the delayed reveal to Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p55-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the cafe  explaining the alliance  the delayed reveal to horikita  it s because for the next year  as class c aims for class a  ichinose and her class s cooperation is essential   indeed  i m serious  in fact  ichinose and i have formed a complete alliance   forming an alliance isn t just about yielding to each other and not fighting   a tightly bound contract can sometimes be a fatal blow   it s more effective when we make it known   for them to learn about it once the wound of the transfer has healed a bit  that will hurt them more deeply  explains the alliance s logic  doubled information  coordinated private points  no binding contract  allowing flexibility  and mutual concession only while the classes are unequal  deliberately delays telling horikita to maximize the psychological damage  ruthless toward horikita   his true goal is not her downfall but her growth  trusting her classmates will help her recover  uses lip service for hashimoto s benefit  reveals their complete alliance  she explains the arrangement of conceding victory to whichever class has fewer points  based on equality and trust  no contract  answers his skeptical questions  hashimoto calls ichinose a  burden  and probes what return she wants  skeptical of the alliance  argues conceding victories throws away opportunities  and that hashimoto would oppose the plan if he weren t invested","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p55-1\">The café: explaining the alliance; the delayed reveal to Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.55–65<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s because for the next year, as Class C aims for Class A, Ichinose and her class&#x27;s cooperation is essential.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Indeed, I&#x27;m serious. In fact, Ichinose and I have formed a complete alliance.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Forming an alliance isn&#x27;t just about yielding to each other and not fighting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A tightly bound contract can sometimes be a fatal blow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s more effective when we make it known.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;for them to learn about it once the wound of the transfer has healed a bit. That will hurt them more deeply.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Explains the alliance&#x27;s logic: doubled information, coordinated Private Points, no binding contract (allowing flexibility), and mutual concession only while the classes are unequal; deliberately delays telling Horikita to maximize the psychological damage.<span class=\"pg\">p.58–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ruthless toward Horikita — his true goal is not her downfall but her growth, trusting her classmates will help her recover; uses lip service for Hashimoto&#x27;s benefit.<span class=\"pg\">p.64–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Reveals their complete alliance; she explains the arrangement of conceding victory to whichever class has fewer points, based on equality and trust, no contract.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Answers his skeptical questions; Hashimoto calls Ichinose a &quot;burden&quot; and probes what return she wants.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Skeptical of the alliance; argues conceding victories throws away opportunities, and that Hashimoto would oppose the plan if he weren&#x27;t invested.<span class=\"pg\">p.58–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p49-1\">← Before: The contract with Hashimoto; reason for transferring via Class A money<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p66-1\">→ After: Aftermath and the confrontation with former classmates<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p55-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hashimoto-masayoshi ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ichinose at the cafe  the alliance explained and defended  sorry to keep you waiting  ayanokouji kun   i found out a little while ago   so  anticipating that  we ve already made detailed arrangements   of course  if the time comes  the alliance will be dissolved   there s no contract  we ve just exchanged promises verbally   no  that s enough for me  just like ayanokouji kun trusts me  i trust him too   having fallen into class d  our backs are against the wall   sorry  hashimoto  but the alliance i want to reap benefits from is based on equality  not subordination   because it s ayanokouji kun s proposal  calm  trustworthy and grown   explains the concession arrangement  insists on a verbal promise over a contract  refuses to pressure hashimoto for a  return  and puts her faith squarely in ayanokoji because the proposal is his  complete alliance with him  trusts him unconditionally and defends him against hashimoto s probing  answered his skeptical questions  hashimoto called her a  burden  and demanded a return for the alliance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p55-1\">Ichinose at the café: the alliance explained and defended<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.55–64<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Sorry to keep you waiting, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;I found out a little while ago.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;So, anticipating that, we&#x27;ve already made detailed arrangements.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course, if the time comes, the alliance will be dissolved.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s no contract. We&#x27;ve just exchanged promises verbally.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, that&#x27;s enough for me. Just like Ayanokouji-kun trusts me, I trust him too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Having fallen into Class D, our backs are against the wall.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, Hashimoto, but the alliance I want to reap benefits from is based on equality, not subordination.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Because it&#x27;s Ayanokouji-kun&#x27;s proposal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm, trustworthy and grown — explains the concession arrangement, insists on a verbal promise over a contract, refuses to pressure Hashimoto for a &quot;return,&quot; and puts her faith squarely in Ayanokōji because the proposal is his.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Complete alliance with him; trusts him unconditionally and defends him against Hashimoto&#x27;s probing.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Answered his skeptical questions; Hashimoto called her a &quot;burden&quot; and demanded a return for the alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.58–64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p37-1\">← Before: Ichinose watches the confrontation with keen interest<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p90-1\">→ After: Ichinose&#x27;s gym meeting with Amasawa; deflecting the probe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p66-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke sudou-ken ike-kanji miyake-akito yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka aftermath and the confrontation with former classmates  i m aware of that  sooner or later  there will be students who voice their opinions against me   i didn t say anything because i wanted to trouble the class   class c was in trouble without sakayanagi  so  i chose to help by transferring in exchange for private points   nothing  times the transfer for immediately after the opening ceremony to maximize class a s shock  tells his former friends the transfer was selfish and for private points   a contrived half truth  since he wanted that reaction  cold and indifferent to their pleas   gives them no real reason  calls his departure voluntary  and accepts hirata s respectful withdrawal  notes he and hirata had been intentionally distancing by first last name  he approaches privately  later respectfully accepts that kiyotaka left on his own free will and departs  having grown to distrust him somewhat  he demands to know why  ayanokoji says there s no meaning in answering  sudo is left frustrated  blames the karuizawa breakup  confused why class c would pay 20 million for him  asks the real reason and notes hasebe was heartbroken  blaming herself  keisei says ayanokoji saved him  he might not have stayed at the school  and asks for the full story","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p66-1\">Aftermath and the confrontation with former classmates<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.66–74<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m aware of that. Sooner or later, there will be students who voice their opinions against me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I didn&#x27;t say anything because I wanted to trouble the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Class C was in trouble without Sakayanagi. So, I chose to help by transferring in exchange for Private Points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Times the transfer for immediately after the opening ceremony to maximize Class A&#x27;s shock; tells his former friends the transfer was selfish and for Private Points — a contrived half-truth, since he wanted that reaction.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cold and indifferent to their pleas — gives them no real reason, calls his departure voluntary, and accepts Hirata&#x27;s respectful withdrawal; notes he and Hirata had been intentionally distancing by first/last name.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He approaches privately; later respectfully accepts that Kiyotaka left on his own free will and departs, having grown to distrust him somewhat.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He demands to know why; Ayanokōji says there&#x27;s no meaning in answering; Sudō is left frustrated.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Blames the Karuizawa breakup; confused why Class C would pay 20 million for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Asks the real reason and notes Hasebe was heartbroken, blaming herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Keisei says Ayanokōji saved him (he might not have stayed at the school) and asks for the full story.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p55-1\">← Before: The café: explaining the alliance; the delayed reveal to Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-1\">→ After: Getting to know Shiraishi; the morning conversation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p66-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke hirata s private talk and respectful acceptance  would you mind changing the location a bit  it seems like people might gather here   sudou kun  if we keep talking here  more and more people will gather  the  i was once saved by you too  line is keisei s  yukimura teruhiko  the translation leaves the exchanges in this stretch unattributed   we have to respect that   is there anything you need to tell the class  calm and mediating   tries to move the confrontation away from onlookers  admits he came to distrust ayanokoji somewhat during the examinations  then respectfully accepts his departure and leaves  addressing him as  kiyotaka  his close friend  once saved by him  now distancing  by first last name  and accepting his choice  holds him back from confronting ayanokoji in public","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p66-1\">Hirata&#x27;s private talk and respectful acceptance<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.66–74<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;Would you mind changing the location a bit? It seems like people might gather here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;Sudou-kun. If we keep talking here, more and more people will gather.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;We have to respect that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The &quot;I was once saved by you too&quot; line is Keisei&#x27;s (Yukimura Teruhiko); the translation leaves the exchanges in this stretch unattributed.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is there anything you need to tell the class?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and mediating — tries to move the confrontation away from onlookers, admits he came to distrust Ayanokōji somewhat during the examinations, then respectfully accepts his departure and leaves, addressing him as &quot;Kiyotaka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His close friend; once saved by him, now distancing (by first/last name) and accepting his choice.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Holds him back from confronting Ayanokōji in public.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p16-1\">← Before: Hirata checks on Chabashira; urges accepting reality<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p106-1\">→ After: Hirata leads the exam discussion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p69-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune ike-kanji sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken sudo demands answers from ayanokoji  hirata  ayanokouji   why did you do it   why the hell did you do that  ayanokouji  why did you transfer classes   wha  are you serious   suzune was relying on you  what kind of face do you plan to make from tomorrow onward  angry and hurt   demands to know why ayanokoji left  slaps ike for the karuizawa joke  tries to rally the others  but is left frustrated when ayanokoji gives no real reason and hirata accepts it  confronts him outside the dorm  gets no satisfying answer  is upset on suzune s behalf   she was relying on ayanokoji  slaps him on the back for joking about the breakup","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p69-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p69-1\">Sudō demands answers from Ayanokōji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.69–74<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Hirata… Ayanokouji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Why did you do it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Why the hell did you do that, Ayanokouji? Why did you transfer classes?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Wha… Are you serious…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Suzune was relying on you. What kind of face do you plan to make from tomorrow onward…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Angry and hurt — demands to know why Ayanokōji left, slaps Ike for the Karuizawa joke, tries to rally the others, but is left frustrated when Ayanokōji gives no real reason and Hirata accepts it.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Confronts him outside the dorm; gets no satisfying answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Is upset on Suzune&#x27;s behalf — she was relying on Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Slaps him on the back for joking about the breakup.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p13-1\">← Before: Sudō&#x27;s theory: Ayanokōji is dodging Karuizawa<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p103-1\">→ After: Sudō&#x27;s concern for Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-miyake-akito-y3v1-p70-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka miyake-akito","q":"miyake akito akito asks  then offers friendship  so  what s the real reason   we re still friends even if you left the class  if you ever encounter any problems  feel free to consult us  holds back anger  asks the real reason  then accepts the departure gracefully   telling ayanokoji they remain friends and offering help  his friend  asks why and pledges continued friendship","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-miyake-akito-y3v1-p70-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html#sc-miyake-akito-y3v1-p70-1\">Akito asks, then offers friendship<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.70–74<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> &quot;So, what&#x27;s the real reason?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> &quot;We&#x27;re still friends even if you left the class. If you ever encounter any problems, feel free to consult us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Holds back anger, asks the real reason, then accepts the departure gracefully — telling Ayanokōji they remain friends and offering help.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His friend; asks why and pledges continued friendship.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-miyake-akito-y3v1-p24-1\">← Before: Akito: not a word beforehand<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"shiraishi-asuka yoshida-kenta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka getting to know shiraishi  the morning conversation arrives 30  minutes early to observe class c  finds shiraishi already at the desk beside his  shiraishi s oaa  academic b   76  physical d  34  adaptability c   57  social c   44  overall c  54  noted beauty mark under her left eye  long blonde hair  headband  calm aura   i didn t expect someone to be here already  you re rather early   since i ve switched classes  it s like i m a transfer student from a different school  rather than being welcomed  i thought it d be better to be the one doing the welcoming   that s only natural   it s too late to start now  couldn t you have opposed and refused my transfer  deliberately mixes truths to probe her  finds it harder to talk than expected  unlike hirata  and learns she holds him in high regard with high expectations  accepts her offer to introduce friends  his new desk neighbor  has a long morning conversation  learns her views  and accepts her offer to meet her friends  yoshida arrives  is needled by shiraishi into retracting his  acknowledge him  demand and helping ayanokoji fit in","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-1\">Getting to know Shiraishi; the morning conversation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.75–84<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives 30+ minutes early to observe Class C; finds Shiraishi already at the desk beside his.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I didn&#x27;t expect someone to be here already. You&#x27;re rather early.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Since I&#x27;ve switched classes, it&#x27;s like I&#x27;m a transfer student from a different school. Rather than being welcomed, I thought it&#x27;d be better to be the one doing the welcoming.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;That&#x27;s only natural.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Shiraishi&#x27;s OAA: Academic B+ (76), Physical D (34), Adaptability C+ (57), Social C− (44), Overall C (54); noted beauty mark under her left eye, long blonde hair, headband, calm aura.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s too late to start now. Couldn&#x27;t you have opposed and refused my transfer?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately mixes truths to probe her, finds it harder to talk than expected (unlike Hirata), and learns she holds him in high regard with high expectations; accepts her offer to introduce friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> His new desk neighbor; has a long morning conversation, learns her views, and accepts her offer to meet her friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Yoshida arrives, is needled by Shiraishi into retracting his &quot;acknowledge him&quot; demand and helping Ayanokōji fit in.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p66-1\">← Before: Aftermath and the confrontation with former classmates<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p85-1\">→ After: Hōsen&#x27;s challenge; Chabashira&#x27;s tailing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p85-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"housen-kazuomi chabashira-sae nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka hosen s challenge  chabashira s tailing  sorry  but i m not interested in fighting   if that s what you re looking for  you should ask ryuuen   nanase seems more capable of being a solid leader than you  housen   i thought you might think that way  chabashira sensei   this transfer is entirely for my own sake  declines hosen s challenge  a  punching bag  search  notes he delegated class leadership to nanase  and repeatedly deflects chabashira s probing about the transfer s true reason  tells her it wasn t because of hoshinomiya and won t disclose his task  second year class d  approaches aggressively  calls him  paisen  wants a fight  and threatens to return for a  sparring partner  his former homeroom teacher has been tailing him in the cold mornings  confronts him  suspects he sacrificed himself over hoshinomiya   he denies it  hosen says he s delegated class matters to her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p85-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p85-1\">Hōsen&#x27;s challenge; Chabashira&#x27;s tailing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.85–89<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Sorry, but I&#x27;m not interested in fighting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;If that&#x27;s what you&#x27;re looking for, you should ask Ryuuen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Nanase seems more capable of being a solid leader than you, Housen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I thought you might think that way, Chabashira-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This transfer is entirely for my own sake.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Declines Hōsen&#x27;s challenge (a &quot;punching bag&quot; search), notes he delegated class leadership to Nanase, and repeatedly deflects Chabashira&#x27;s probing about the transfer&#x27;s true reason; tells her it wasn&#x27;t because of Hoshinomiya and won&#x27;t disclose his task.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Second-year Class D; approaches aggressively, calls him &quot;Paisen,&quot; wants a fight, and threatens to return for a &quot;sparring partner.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.85–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> His former homeroom teacher has been tailing him in the cold mornings; confronts him, suspects he sacrificed himself over Hoshinomiya — he denies it.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Hōsen says he&#x27;s delegated class matters to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-1\">← Before: Getting to know Shiraishi; the morning conversation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p108-1\">→ After: Class C entrusts the exam to Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p87-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hoshinomiya-chie chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira tails ayanokoji  asks whether the transfer was on her account appears at the mall and pulls ayanokoji aside  she admits her colleagues had noticed him and that hoshinomiya s issue is resolved   come with me for a moment   i wanted to talk to you  as your homeroom teacher  no  as your former homeroom teacher  i thought it might be inappropriate to carelessly make contact  but i couldn t help wanting to check something   you noticed   that doesn t matter  what i want to hear about is the class transfer  the transfer matter  what were you thinking when you decided to transfer without telling anyone   isn t there something inconvenient  something that forced you to transfer   is it really because of me  because i was troubled with chie s problem  did you sacrifice yourself to solve it   what s the reason then  why do something so meaningless   it doesn t seem like you re simply being considerate   yes   understood  i see  sorry for taking your time  quietly relieved yet still chasing answers   stays calm in the open but visibly cannot accept losing him without knowing why  ayanokoji notes she might still share the talk with others  tails him from the dorm  he tells her the transfer was not on her account and that it was decided even before hoshinomiya s issue surfaced  her trouble is what chabashira feared had cost them ayanokoji  ayanokoji rates her tailing skills as on par with morishita s    and to put it nicely  they weren t good","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p87-1\">Chabashira tails Ayanokōji; asks whether the transfer was on her account<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.87–89<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears at the mall and pulls Ayanokōji aside; she admits her colleagues had noticed him and that Hoshinomiya&#x27;s issue is resolved.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Come with me for a moment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;…I wanted to talk to you. As your homeroom teacher… no, as your former homeroom teacher, I thought it might be inappropriate to carelessly make contact, but I couldn&#x27;t help wanting to check something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;…You noticed?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That doesn&#x27;t matter. What I want to hear about is the class transfer… the transfer matter. What were you thinking when you decided to transfer without telling anyone…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Isn&#x27;t there something inconvenient… something that forced you to transfer?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is it really because of me? Because I was troubled with Chie&#x27;s problem… Did you sacrifice yourself to solve it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What&#x27;s the reason then? Why do something so meaningless…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It doesn&#x27;t seem like you&#x27;re simply being considerate…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yes…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Understood. I see… sorry for taking your time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Quietly relieved yet still chasing answers — stays calm in the open but visibly cannot accept losing him without knowing why; Ayanokōji notes she might still share the talk with others.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Tails him from the dorm; he tells her the transfer was not on her account and that it was decided even before Hoshinomiya&#x27;s issue surfaced.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Her trouble is what Chabashira feared had cost them Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji rates her tailing skills as on par with Morishita&#x27;s — &quot;and to put it nicely, they weren&#x27;t good.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p16-1\">← Before: Chabashira announces the transfer; ends the homeroom with a warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-amasawa-ichika-y3v1-p90-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka amasawa-ichika","q":"amasawa ichika amasawa probes ichinose about ayanokoji calls out to ichinose in keyaki mall  smiling innocently  brings up the gym and ayanokoji   did you go to the gym today   but i tend to spend a lot of money  so the monthly expense is kind of painful   it does matter  i like ayanokouji senpai a lot   oh  i mean i like him as a senpai  not that there are any romantic feelings   actually  i really do love him in that way   i m pretty sharp  you know   after all  you ve slept with ayanokouji senpai  right   you re saying you re that special cake  but you re dangerously full of yourself   hold on  did ayanokouji senpai really talk to you about the white room  ichinose senpai   shoot  i m the one getting carried away here  playful but venomous   feigns innocence then turns hostile  probing ichinose with a  bomb  question about sleeping with ayanokoji to see her agitation  is outmaneuvered when ichinose mentions the white room  stiffens  then realizes she was the one countered  probes her about her relationship with ayanokoji  ends up respecting her more  claims to love him  in that way  the reason she remains at the school is to make ayanokoji happy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y3v1-p90-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html#sc-amasawa-ichika-y3v1-p90-1\">Amasawa probes Ichinose about Ayanokōji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.90–97<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Calls out to Ichinose in Keyaki Mall, smiling innocently; brings up the gym and Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;Did you go to the gym today?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;But I tend to spend a lot of money, so the monthly expense is kind of painful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;It does matter. I like Ayanokouji-senpai a lot.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, I mean I like him as a senpai, not that there are any romantic feelings~&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Actually, I really do love him in that way.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m pretty sharp, you know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;After all… you&#x27;ve slept with Ayanokouji-senpai, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re saying you&#x27;re that special cake, but you&#x27;re dangerously full of yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hold on. Did Ayanokouji-senpai really talk to you about the White Room, Ichinose-senpai?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…Shoot. I&#x27;m the one getting carried away here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Playful but venomous — feigns innocence then turns hostile, probing Ichinose with a &quot;bomb&quot; question about sleeping with Ayanokōji to see her agitation; is outmaneuvered when Ichinose mentions the White Room, stiffens, then realizes she was the one countered.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Probes her about her relationship with Ayanokōji; ends up respecting her more.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Claims to love him &quot;in that way&quot;; the reason she remains at the school is to make Ayanokōji happy.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p90-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ichinose s gym meeting with amasawa  deflecting the probe descends to the first floor after the gym  is called out by amasawa ichika  class 2 a   yeah  just for about an hour though   really  if you re interested  why not try it out or come for a visit   me  i m not in that kind of relationship with ayanokouji kun   it s true  so don t worry   it was you who asked me not to lie  amasawa san   ayanokouji kun and i are bound by a strong bond  that s all there is to it   that s why you shouldn t eat too much   there are no more secrets between me and ayanokouji kun   like matters  for example  about the white room   i can t tell you that  it might be the same as you  or even more  bluffs that ayanokoji told her about the  white room    a term she only overheard during the second year island exam   to probe whether amasawa is connected to it  confirms amasawa likely originated there when she stiffens at the word  calm and strategically canny beneath the mature smile   refuses to be rattled by increasingly venomous questions  turns amasawa s  don t lie  against her  and learns something new about ayanokoji through the exchange  is probed by her about her relationship with ayanokoji  counters by bluffing knowledge of the white room  defends their  strong bond  and denies dating  uses a white room bluff to gauge amasawa","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p90-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p90-1\">Ichinose&#x27;s gym meeting with Amasawa; deflecting the probe<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.90–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Descends to the first floor after the gym; is called out by Amasawa Ichika (Class 2-A).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Yeah, just for about an hour though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Really? If you&#x27;re interested, why not try it out or come for a visit?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Me? I&#x27;m not in that kind of relationship with Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s true, so don&#x27;t worry.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It was you who asked me not to lie, Amasawa-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun and I are bound by a strong bond. That&#x27;s all there is to it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s why you shouldn&#x27;t eat too much.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There are no more secrets between me and Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Like matters, for example, about the White Room.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can&#x27;t tell you that. It might be the same as you, or even more.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Bluffs that Ayanokōji told her about the &quot;White Room&quot; — a term she only overheard during the second-year island exam — to probe whether Amasawa is connected to it; confirms Amasawa likely originated there when she stiffens at the word.<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and strategically canny beneath the mature smile — refuses to be rattled by increasingly venomous questions, turns Amasawa&#x27;s &quot;don&#x27;t lie&quot; against her, and learns something new about Ayanokōji through the exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Is probed by her about her relationship with Ayanokōji; counters by bluffing knowledge of the White Room.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Defends their &quot;strong bond&quot; and denies dating; uses a White Room bluff to gauge Amasawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p55-1\">← Before: Ichinose at the café: the alliance explained and defended<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p164-1\">→ After: Ichinose&#x27;s confrontation with Karuizawa; a new resolve<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p98-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka matsushita-chiaki sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune a week on  grief  the exam announcement  and self loathing sits alone before homeroom  a week after the transfer  observes the class adapting as if nothing happened   they were trying to alter their two years with ayanokouji kun as if it had never happened   was this class not good enough   if i had been more reliable  could he have stayed without transferring   did you hear me  horikita   sorry  yes  it s okay  i m listening    a lie  she heard nothing heartbroken and unable to focus   matsushita smiles less  sudo gets irritable  and she herself is  desperately trying to maintain class a s image by acting calmly  realizes with self loathing that she feels relief at not facing ayanokoji  class d is their opponent  her grief over his absence grows daily  regrets the feelings at the celebration party that never reached him  notices she smiles and talks less  notices he gets irritated over trivial matters again  he checks on her when she zones out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p98-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p98-1\">A week on: grief, the exam announcement, and self-loathing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.98–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits alone before homeroom, a week after the transfer; observes the class adapting as if nothing happened.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;They were trying to alter their two years with Ayanokouji-kun as if it had never happened.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Was this class not good enough?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;If I had been more reliable, could he have stayed without transferring?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Did you hear me? Horikita.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Sorry, yes. It&#x27;s okay, I&#x27;m listening.&quot; — a lie; she heard nothing<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Heartbroken and unable to focus — Matsushita smiles less, Sudō gets irritable, and she herself is &quot;desperately trying to maintain Class A&#x27;s image by acting calmly&quot;; realizes with self-loathing that she feels relief at not facing Ayanokōji (Class D is their opponent).<span class=\"pg\">p.98–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her grief over his absence grows daily; regrets the feelings at the celebration party that never reached him.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Notices she smiles and talks less.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Notices he gets irritated over trivial matters again; he checks on her when she zones out.<span class=\"pg\">p.98, 106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p34-1\">← Before: The café confrontation; Ayanokōji&#x27;s cold exposure<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p126-1\">→ After: The bench with Kushida; the collapse in her room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p103-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken sudo s concern for horikita  looks like it s going to be a tough fight   are you okay   that s true  but  you re still worried about ayanokouji  aren t you   it s impossible not to worry  but don t keep it all to yourself  stern about the exam but gentle with horikita   notices she s preoccupied  puts a hand on her shoulder  and urges her not to bottle up her worry about ayanokoji  checks on her when she spaces out  knows she s still worried about him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p103-1\">Sudō&#x27;s concern for Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.103–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Looks like it&#x27;s going to be a tough fight…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Are you okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;That&#x27;s true, but… you&#x27;re still worried about Ayanokouji, aren&#x27;t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s impossible not to worry, but don&#x27;t keep it all to yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Stern about the exam but gentle with Horikita — notices she&#x27;s preoccupied, puts a hand on her shoulder, and urges her not to bottle up her worry about Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Checks on her when she spaces out.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Knows she&#x27;s still worried about him.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y3v1-p69-1\">← Before: Sudō demands answers from Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p106-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke hirata leads the exam discussion  how we use the penalty points is important  focusing on targeting students likely to score high and getting it wrong is scary   we should discuss what to do about the special exam    his message to horikita takes the lead in the class discussion on penalty points and later messages the isolated horikita to pull her back to reality and focus on the exam  messages her about the exam  reaching her when she s collapsed on her bed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p106-1\">Hirata leads the exam discussion<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.106–107, 133<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;How we use the penalty points is important… Focusing on targeting students likely to score high and getting it wrong is scary.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;[We should discuss what to do about the special exam.]&quot; — his message to Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes the lead in the class discussion on penalty points and later messages the isolated Horikita to pull her back to reality and focus on the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Messages her about the exam, reaching her when she&#x27;s collapsed on her bed.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v1-p66-1\">← Before: Hirata&#x27;s private talk and respectful acceptance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y3v1-p107-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko yukimura s advice on the small group battles  i think it s better not to rely solely on the oaa evaluations for the small group battles   a student who s extremely weak in one subject but strong in others can still score high  suggests leveraging detailed  class only knowledge of who is strong in which subjects   noting oaa is only an average across all subjects","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y3v1-p107-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y3v1-p107-1\">Yukimura&#x27;s advice on the small-group battles<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> &quot;I think it&#x27;s better not to rely solely on the OAA evaluations for the small-group battles.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> &quot;A student who&#x27;s extremely weak in one subject but strong in others can still score high.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Suggests leveraging detailed, class-only knowledge of who is strong in which subjects — noting OAA is only an average across all subjects.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p108-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi shimazaki-ikkei sanada-kousei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka class c entrusts the exam to ayanokoji  i can t guarantee our victory or defeat  but if you entrust me with it  i intend to give it my all   if you entrust it to me  i ll do my best  hashimoto pushes to leave the exam to him  shimazaki objects  wanting class discussion  sanada proposes a compromise   test him by seeing whether he can predict the opponent s small group participants and penalty distribution  deliberately plays it safe with his words  unlike his confident opening ceremony speech  to avoid a unanimous delegation  accepting the  test  framing  pushes fiercely for ayanokoji to lead  agitated about being excluded from the transfer talks  skeptical  doesn t want to entrust the exam to him  proposes judging him by his prediction accuracy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p108-1\">Class C entrusts the exam to Ayanokōji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.108–110<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sanada-kousei.html\">Sanada Kōsei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I can&#x27;t guarantee our victory or defeat, but if you entrust me with it, I intend to give it my all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;If you entrust it to me, I&#x27;ll do my best.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Hashimoto pushes to leave the exam to him; Shimazaki objects, wanting class discussion; Sanada proposes a compromise — test him by seeing whether he can predict the opponent&#x27;s small-group participants and penalty distribution.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately plays it safe with his words (unlike his confident opening-ceremony speech) to avoid a unanimous delegation, accepting the &quot;test&quot; framing.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Pushes fiercely for Ayanokōji to lead; agitated about being excluded from the transfer talks.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Skeptical; doesn&#x27;t want to entrust the exam to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sanada Kōsei<\/b> Proposes judging him by his prediction accuracy.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p85-1\">← Before: Hōsen&#x27;s challenge; Chabashira&#x27;s tailing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p112-1\">→ After: The café strategy: penalty points, spies, and withheld info<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p112-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"morishita-ai yamamura-miki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the cafe strategy  penalty points  spies  and withheld info  i ve already given yamamura a heads up  it s better for her to keep her distance from me for a while   i can t talk about that at this point yet  saying anything careless here and having them taken at face value would be troublesome   i don t know a thing about it   there s still time until the exam  all i have to do is come up with a winning strategy by then   i have no intention of participating in the small group battles in this special exam   there s an eighty to ninety percent chance ryuuen will impose multiple penalty points on me  identifies komiya yamawaki and two first years  including takikura  as ryuen s surveillance   the first years  phones placed face down toward them  never checked  deduces ryuen has been recruiting first years within a week  withholds real analysis  only shares  safe  information  reasons that ryuen will target him so he needn t participate  and reads the enemy s spy network sharply  discusses yamamura  has told her to keep her distance  morishita joins as a listener and needles him  has told her to keep her distance so she isn t stressed by the attention around him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p112-1\">The café strategy: penalty points, spies, and withheld info<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.112–121<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamamura-miki.html\">Yamamura Miki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ve already given Yamamura a heads-up. It&#x27;s better for her to keep her distance from me for a while.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I can&#x27;t talk about that at this point yet. Saying anything careless here and having them taken at face value would be troublesome.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t know a thing about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s still time until the exam. All I have to do is come up with a winning strategy by then.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have no intention of participating in the small-group battles in this special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s an eighty to ninety percent chance Ryuuen will impose multiple penalty points on me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Identifies Komiya/Yamawaki and two first-years (including Takikura) as Ryūen&#x27;s surveillance — the first-years&#x27; phones placed face-down toward them, never checked; deduces Ryūen has been recruiting first-years within a week.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Withholds real analysis (only shares &quot;safe&quot; information), reasons that Ryūen will target him so he needn&#x27;t participate, and reads the enemy&#x27;s spy network sharply.<span class=\"pg\">p.119–121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Discusses Yamamura (has told her to keep her distance); Morishita joins as a listener and needles him.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamamura Miki<\/b> Has told her to keep her distance so she isn&#x27;t stressed by the attention around him.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p108-1\">← Before: Class C entrusts the exam to Ayanokōji<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p122-1\">→ After: Ryūen and Ishizaki confront him at the café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p122-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ryuen and ishizaki confront him at the cafe  there s no particular reason  sakayanagi left  and class c came to help me transfer   does my transferring to class c cause any inconvenience to you   my class expects results in the upcoming special exam  please go easy on us   i intend to    on seeing shiina faces ryuen calmly  gives the same  no reason  line  and privately notes ryuen welcomed the transfer as a better stage to defeat him  has deliberately avoided the library and decides to see hiyori after the exam  he comes to the cafe with ishizaki and albert  welcomes the transfer because now ayanokoji leads class c directly  and vows to play every card  explodes demanding why he transferred  leaves frustrated  tells him to meet shiina  who s been down  ishizaki s message about shiina being down is what ayanokoji uses to decide to visit the library after the exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p122-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p122-1\">Ryūen and Ishizaki confront him at the café<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.122–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;There&#x27;s no particular reason. Sakayanagi left, and Class C came to help me transfer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Does my transferring to Class C cause any inconvenience to you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;My class expects results in the upcoming special exam. Please go easy on us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I intend to.&quot; — on seeing Shiina<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Faces Ryūen calmly, gives the same &quot;no reason&quot; line, and privately notes Ryūen welcomed the transfer as a better stage to defeat him; has deliberately avoided the library and decides to see Hiyori after the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He comes to the café with Ishizaki and Albert; welcomes the transfer because now Ayanokōji leads Class C directly, and vows to play every card.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Explodes demanding why he transferred; leaves frustrated, tells him to meet Shiina (who&#x27;s been down).<span class=\"pg\">p.122–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ishizaki&#x27;s message about Shiina being down is what Ayanokōji uses to decide to visit the library after the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p112-1\">← Before: The café strategy: penalty points, spies, and withheld info<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-1\">→ After: The Sunday karaoke outing; Nishikawa&#x27;s warnings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p126-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the bench with kushida  the collapse in her room sits gloomily on a bench on the way back to the dorm  kushida stops and needles her   why the questioning tone   you re just incredibly clingy  aren t you   i m not in the mood to do anything right now   ambushing him in a place like this doing such a thing  there s no way he d be happy about it   again  he made me cry   why  devastated and stuck   kushida s cold words make her realize she was  playing the part of a pitiful horikita  goes home  collapses on her bed in uniform  cries again  and dwells on wishing she could turn back time to grab ayanokoji s arm  kushida sees through her  calls her clingy  criticizes her gloomy face as bad for morale  and leaves cold words  i doubt he ll care  kushida says ibuki has been coming to her for food since horikita stopped cooking  hirata messages her to discuss the exam  pulling her slightly back to reality","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p126-1\">The bench with Kushida; the collapse in her room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.126–135<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits gloomily on a bench on the way back to the dorm; Kushida stops and needles her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Why the questioning tone?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;re just incredibly clingy, aren&#x27;t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m not in the mood to do anything right now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Ambushing him in a place like this—doing such a thing… there&#x27;s no way he&#x27;d be happy about it…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;…Again, he made me cry…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Why…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Devastated and stuck — Kushida&#x27;s cold words make her realize she was &quot;playing the part of a pitiful Horikita&quot;; goes home, collapses on her bed in uniform, cries again, and dwells on wishing she could turn back time to grab Ayanokōji&#x27;s arm.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida sees through her, calls her clingy, criticizes her gloomy face as bad for morale, and leaves cold words (&quot;I doubt he&#x27;ll care&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.126–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Kushida says Ibuki has been coming to her for food since Horikita stopped cooking.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata messages her to discuss the exam, pulling her slightly back to reality.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p98-1\">← Before: A week on: grief, the exam announcement, and self-loathing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p180-1\">→ After: Class A&#x27;s loss; Horikita&#x27;s regret<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p126-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ninomiya-yui kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo kushida needles the gloomy horikita buys a cafe au lait to go  spots horikita gloomy on a bench  and stops   i m not going to ask what you re doing here  you re waiting to bump into ayanokouji kun by pretending it s a coincidence  aren t you   no  it s totally obvious   i d like to leave you alone  but i can t overlook such a gloomy face   even in these circumstances  a class leader is supposed to win regardless   you can wait here for ayanokouji kun to come back  but  i doubt he ll care  cynical but pragmatic   her true nature exposed  increasingly isolated and short tempered  needling horikita  she still wants her class leader to win  needed for her own class a graduation  and delivers cold parting advice  sees through her  criticizes her state  urges her to focus on the exam  then leaves coldly  knows horikita is waiting for him  doubts he cares  politely says goodbye to the class 3 d student  smiling until she s out of earshot   the two faced act","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p126-1\">Kushida needles the gloomy Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.126–132<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Buys a café au lait to go, spots Horikita gloomy on a bench, and stops.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ninomiya-yui.html\">Ninomiya Yui<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m not going to ask what you&#x27;re doing here. You&#x27;re waiting to bump into Ayanokouji-kun by pretending it&#x27;s a coincidence, aren&#x27;t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;No, it&#x27;s totally obvious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;d like to leave you alone, but I can&#x27;t overlook such a gloomy face.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even in these circumstances, a class leader is supposed to win regardless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You can wait here for Ayanokouji-kun to come back. But… I doubt he&#x27;ll care.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cynical but pragmatic — her true nature exposed, increasingly isolated and short-tempered; needling Horikita, she still wants her class leader to win (needed for her own Class A graduation), and delivers cold parting advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sees through her, criticizes her state, urges her to focus on the exam, then leaves coldly.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Knows Horikita is waiting for him; doubts he cares.<span class=\"pg\">p.127, 131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ninomiya Yui<\/b> Politely says goodbye to the Class 3-D student, smiling until she&#x27;s out of earshot — the two-faced act.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p25-1\">← Before: Kushida: Ayanokōji was more important than assumed<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p216-1\">→ After: Kushida&#x27;s dusk meeting: Ayanokōji&#x27;s offer of betrayal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p136-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune ishizaki-daichi ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki s disdain and horikita s cooking  why are you asking me  just do what you want   why not just give up  losing the opportunity to gain about a hundred class points isn t a big deal  right   i don t care about that story   don t ask me  you shouldn t even try to understand his thoughts   i get really annoyed just talking about him  i truly hate him   it s annoying   haaaaaaa  she s not my friend  combative and blunt   recommends giving up the academic exam  refuses to engage with ayanokoji  having learned it leads to complications  genuinely hates him  and denies being horikita s friend despite eating at her room  refuses to think about him  says she truly hates him  has been coming to her room for food but says they aren t friends  notes she hasn t recovered  bickers with him over food and ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p136-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p136-1\">Ibuki&#x27;s disdain and Horikita&#x27;s cooking<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.136–143<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;Why are you asking me? Just do what you want.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;Why not just give up? Losing the opportunity to gain about a hundred class points isn&#x27;t a big deal, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t care about that story.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don&#x27;t ask me. You shouldn&#x27;t even try to understand his thoughts.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I get really annoyed just talking about him. I truly hate him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s annoying.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Haaaaaaa? She&#x27;s not my friend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Combative and blunt — recommends giving up the academic exam, refuses to engage with Ayanokōji (having learned it leads to complications), genuinely hates him, and denies being Horikita&#x27;s friend despite eating at her room.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Refuses to think about him; says she truly hates him.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Has been coming to her room for food but says they aren&#x27;t friends; notes she hasn&#x27;t recovered.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Bickers with him over food and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p207-1\">→ After: Ibuki kicks Horikita out of frustration<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y3v1-p136-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei katsuragi weighs the penalty point plan  this special exam won t be easy  no  i should say  also  this time   it was made for the class  in fact  students who are taking these seriously have already seen steady improvements   to have a high chance of winning  we d want to take away an additional three hundred points  that would require about 15 million private points   even then  there s no absolute guarantee   we should start off with hashimoto  and it also seems wise to pay special attention to yamamura  serious and responsible   gave the class study assignments  calculates the cost of victory  15 million  warns about the risk of wasted funds and information leaks  and heads off to act  feeling responsible for the class s academic performance  debates the plan and ultimately supports going all out  urges him to study  frustrated by his lack of effort  doubts whether he can surpass sakayanagi  recognizes his calmness and sharpness","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y3v1-p136-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y3v1-p136-1\">Katsuragi weighs the penalty-point plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.136–145<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> &quot;This special exam won&#x27;t be easy. No, I should say &#x27;also&#x27; this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> &quot;It was made for the class. In fact, students who are taking these seriously have already seen steady improvements.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> &quot;To have a high chance of winning… we&#x27;d want to take away an additional three hundred points. That would require about 15 million private points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even then, there&#x27;s no absolute guarantee.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should start off with Hashimoto, and it also seems wise to pay special attention to Yamamura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Serious and responsible — gave the class study assignments, calculates the cost of victory (~15 million), warns about the risk of wasted funds and information leaks, and heads off to act, feeling responsible for the class&#x27;s academic performance.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Debates the plan and ultimately supports going all out.<span class=\"pg\">p.139–144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Urges him to study; frustrated by his lack of effort.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Doubts whether he can surpass Sakayanagi; recognizes his calmness and sharpness.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p139-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei ibuki-mio ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ryuen s camp plans to crush class c s first victory  there s no cure for stupidity  besides  there s no need to play on their turf   that s where my ultimate goal lies    on wanting a formidable opponent  well  if you only look at the returns you can see  sure  that might be the case   this is an exam we re expected to lose  but that also means it s an exam they absolutely cannot afford to lose   if we can strike them down during his first exam  his maiden voyage  it will be a bigger advantage than the actual class point difference   i ve decided how i ll fight  aggressive but calculating   plans to pour private points into penalty points  even  15 million  not just for class points but to shatter ayanokoji s  first victory  and momentum  wants to test whether the  impossible  prediction can be done  sees him as a formidable opponent  wants to strike down his first exam as leader  believes he ll take the exam seriously and may see through their five participants  debates the plan with him  katsuragi estimates  15 million needed and urges against a half hearted approach  she recommends giving up  discusses ayanokoji and horikita  says she truly hates him  wants deep fried pasta  surprised at the cost","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p139-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p139-1\">Ryūen&#x27;s camp plans to crush Class C&#x27;s first victory<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.139–144<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;There&#x27;s no cure for stupidity. Besides, there&#x27;s no need to play on their turf.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;That&#x27;s where my ultimate goal lies.&quot; — on wanting a formidable opponent<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Well, if you only look at the returns you can see, sure, that might be the case.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is an exam we&#x27;re expected to lose. But that also means it&#x27;s an exam they absolutely cannot afford to lose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If we can strike them down during his first exam, his maiden voyage, it will be a bigger advantage than the actual Class Point difference.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…I&#x27;ve decided how I&#x27;ll fight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Aggressive but calculating — plans to pour Private Points into penalty points (even ~15 million) not just for Class Points but to shatter Ayanokōji&#x27;s &quot;first victory&quot; and momentum; wants to test whether the &quot;impossible&quot; prediction can be done.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Sees him as a formidable opponent; wants to strike down his first exam as leader; believes he&#x27;ll take the exam seriously and may see through their five participants.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Debates the plan with him; Katsuragi estimates ~15 million needed and urges against a half-hearted approach.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> She recommends giving up; discusses Ayanokōji and Horikita; says she truly hates him.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Wants deep-fried pasta; surprised at the cost.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p142-1\">→ After: Horikita&#x27;s state discussed; info-leak precautions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p142-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hashimoto-masayoshi yamamura-miki ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru horikita s state discussed  info leak precautions  i don t think she s recovered  she turns me away when i come  and she always has a gloomy expression   good  she should just lose miserably   we should start off with hashimoto  and it also seems wise to pay special attention to yamamura    katsuragi ibuki reports she hasn t recovered from the transfer  ryuen is pleased at the prospect of class a stumbling  identified as the primary information leak risk to watch  katsuragi flags her as someone to watch despite ibuki not knowing her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p142-1\">Horikita&#x27;s state discussed; info-leak precautions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.142–144<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamamura-miki.html\">Yamamura Miki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t think she&#x27;s recovered. She turns me away when I come, and she always has a gloomy expression.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Good. She should just lose miserably.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;We should start off with Hashimoto, and it also seems wise to pay special attention to Yamamura.&quot; — Katsuragi<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ibuki reports she hasn&#x27;t recovered from the transfer; Ryūen is pleased at the prospect of Class A stumbling.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Identified as the primary information-leak risk to watch.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamamura Miki<\/b> Katsuragi flags her as someone to watch despite Ibuki not knowing her.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p139-1\">← Before: Ryūen&#x27;s camp plans to crush Class C&#x27;s first victory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p190-1\">→ After: Ryūen&#x27;s &quot;winner&#x27;s interview&quot; and defeat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"yoshida-kenta nishikawa-ryouko shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the sunday karaoke outing  nishikawa s warnings meets yoshida outside the dorm for the outing  yoshida has been waiting since 9 30 for a 10 30 meeting   that rumor s real    yoshida nishikawa joins in place of shiraishi initially  warns that shiraishi is the  hundred man slayer   romantically involved with a hundred guys    advice  for ayanokouji kun too   i ve come to respect her  it s honestly amazing for someone my age to be involved with a hundred people  reads yoshida s infatuation calmly  learning about romance through karuizawa  probes the class s view of hashimoto  and refuses nishikawa s bait to become shiraishi s 101st   because word could reach yoshida and hinder his class c battles  confirms he likes shiraishi  asks about the class and hashimoto s reputation  she teases him about shiraishi and makes a suggestive offer he refuses  she ends up reconsidering her impression of him with something like hostility  sits beside her in the karaoke l seating  she touches his hand  examines his long fingers nails  and treats him as an interesting experimental subject  like a guinea pig in a small box","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-1\">The Sunday karaoke outing; Nishikawa&#x27;s warnings<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.146–154<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Yoshida outside the dorm for the outing; Yoshida has been waiting since 9:30 for a 10:30 meeting.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nishikawa-ryouko.html\">Nishikawa Ryōko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;That rumor&#x27;s real…?&quot; — Yoshida<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ve come to respect her. It&#x27;s honestly amazing for someone my age to be involved with a hundred people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Nishikawa joins in place of Shiraishi initially; warns that Shiraishi is the &quot;Hundred-Man Slayer&quot; (romantically involved with a hundred guys) — advice &quot;for Ayanokouji-kun too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148–150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Yoshida&#x27;s infatuation calmly (learning about romance through Karuizawa), probes the class&#x27;s view of Hashimoto, and refuses Nishikawa&#x27;s bait to become Shiraishi&#x27;s 101st — because word could reach Yoshida and hinder his Class C battles.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Confirms he likes Shiraishi; asks about the class and Hashimoto&#x27;s reputation.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nishikawa Ryōko<\/b> She teases him about Shiraishi and makes a suggestive offer he refuses; she ends up reconsidering her impression of him with something like hostility.<span class=\"pg\">p.148–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Sits beside her in the karaoke L-seating; she touches his hand, examines his long fingers/nails, and treats him as an interesting experimental subject, like a guinea pig in a small box.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p122-1\">← Before: Ryūen and Ishizaki confront him at the café<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p156-1\">→ After: The eraser-crumb prank; Shiraishi signals the timing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p146-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka shiraishi-asuka morishita-ai","q":"morishita ai morishita s eraser crumb prank and  jeanne d arc  defense  looking behind you during class  even during the self study period  is something only a naughty  naughty student would do   staring at my face from such a close distance  what a pervert   bullying  what a laughable accusation   would you call it bullying if a kitten messes with a lion   what i m doing  if i must say  is similar to jeanne d arc   as long as evil exists in this world  it s my duty to keep fighting  playful and eccentric   rubs an eraser on the desk and flicks the crumbs at ayanokoji s head during class  plays ignorant when caught  and absurdly frames herself as jeanne d arc fighting evil  the physically superior ayanokoji as the  lion  pranks him with eraser crumbs  caught red handed  shiraishi helps catch her and finds the exchange cute","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p146-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html#sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p146-1\">Morishita&#x27;s eraser-crumb prank and &quot;Jeanne d&#x27;Arc&quot; defense<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.146–162<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;Looking behind you during class, even during the self-study period, is something only a naughty, naughty student would do.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;Staring at my face from such a close distance, what a pervert.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;Bullying? What a laughable accusation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Would you call it bullying if a kitten messes with a lion?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What I&#x27;m doing, if I must say, is similar to Jeanne d&#x27;Arc.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;As long as evil exists in this world, it&#x27;s my duty to keep fighting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Playful and eccentric — rubs an eraser on the desk and flicks the crumbs at Ayanokōji&#x27;s head during class, plays ignorant when caught, and absurdly frames herself as Jeanne d&#x27;Arc fighting evil (the physically superior Ayanokōji as the &quot;lion&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.146–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Pranks him with eraser crumbs; caught red-handed.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Shiraishi helps catch her and finds the exchange cute.<span class=\"pg\">p.161–162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p41-1\">← Before: Morishita seats, needles and vets Ayanokōji<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p261-1\">→ After: &quot;Gatling Gun&quot;: the eraser-shaving battlefield<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p156-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"shiraishi-asuka morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the eraser crumb prank  shiraishi signals the timing during self study  feels an uncomfortable sensation in his hair   morishita behind him is rubbing an eraser on the desk and throwing crumbs at his head   you saved me  shiraishi  thanks to you telling me the timing  i caught her red handed  shiraishi silently signals the timing of the eraser taps by pointing at the floor and tapping her desk  he grabs morishita s clenched fist and finds the worn eraser  sharp sensing and composed   uses shiraishi s silent cues to catch morishita  declines to call it  bullying  and learns sugio had given up his seat because of the same trouble  she silently signals the prank s timing to help him  he thanks her and calls her  impressive  catches her throwing eraser crumbs  she plays ignorant and justifies it as  jeanne d arc  defeating evil","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p156-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p156-1\">The eraser-crumb prank; Shiraishi signals the timing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.156–162<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">During self-study, feels an uncomfortable sensation in his hair — Morishita behind him is rubbing an eraser on the desk and throwing crumbs at his head.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;You saved me, Shiraishi. Thanks to you telling me the timing, I caught her red-handed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Shiraishi silently signals the timing of the eraser-taps by pointing at the floor and tapping her desk; he grabs Morishita&#x27;s clenched fist and finds the worn eraser.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sharp-sensing and composed — uses Shiraishi&#x27;s silent cues to catch Morishita, declines to call it &quot;bullying,&quot; and learns Sugio had given up his seat because of the same trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> She silently signals the prank&#x27;s timing to help him; he thanks her and calls her &quot;impressive.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Catches her throwing eraser crumbs; she plays ignorant and justifies it as &quot;Jeanne d&#x27;Arc&quot; defeating evil.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-1\">← Before: The Sunday karaoke outing; Nishikawa&#x27;s warnings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p189-1\">→ After: The aftermath: Shimazaki&#x27;s challenge and Ayanokōji&#x27;s true plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p163-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei karuizawa s heartbreak  confronting ichinose about ayanokoji walks to school alone on exam day  having not smiled since the breakup  sees ayanokoji sitting on a bench   from the time she parted with ayanokouji until this very day  karuizawa hasn t been able to smile even once   are you  uh  are you and ayanokouji kun  dating   me  no way    ichinose heartbroken and jealous but stubbornly attending school   she presses ichinose about dating ayanokoji  can t take the denial at face value  and is both relieved and tortured  ultimately hides in the bushes  unseen  as ichinose walks off with him  interrogates her about ayanokoji  senses her popularity and that she knows his secrets  asks her for help as a  rival  and is quietly refused  still in love with her ex  observes he shows no lingering attachment and walks away with ichinose without looking back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p163-1\">Karuizawa&#x27;s heartbreak; confronting Ichinose about Ayanokōji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.163–173<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks to school alone on exam day, having not smiled since the breakup; sees Ayanokōji sitting on a bench.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;From the time she parted with Ayanokouji until this very day, Karuizawa hasn&#x27;t been able to smile even once.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;Are you… uh, are you and Ayanokouji-kun… dating…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;Me? No way.&quot; — Ichinose<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Heartbroken and jealous but stubbornly attending school — she presses Ichinose about dating Ayanokōji, can&#x27;t take the denial at face value, and is both relieved and tortured; ultimately hides in the bushes, unseen, as Ichinose walks off with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.163–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Interrogates her about Ayanokōji; senses her popularity and that she knows his secrets; asks her for help as a &quot;rival&quot; and is quietly refused.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Still in love with her ex; observes he shows no lingering attachment and walks away with Ichinose without looking back.<span class=\"pg\">p.163–173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p14-1\">← Before: Karuizawa after the breakup, questioned about the transfer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p209-1\">→ After: Karuizawa finds Horikita; sharing her painful past<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p164-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ichinose s confrontation with karuizawa  a new resolve encounters karuizawa on the way to school  reveals she knows her routine  7 50 am  and that ayanokoji waits on the bench to meet her   popular  i m just greeting my friends  like i did with you   me  no way  there s no way ayanokouji kun would date me   it s really true  ayanokouji kun and i are not in that kind of relationship   perhaps he s different from your average person  is that what you wanted to say   you know  don t you  karuizawa san  that i like ayanokouji kun   i guess i m more about giving than receiving   sorry  i take back what i said earlier  maybe i can t help you   he s waiting to meet with me at this time  kind but newly decisive   admits she likes ayanokoji  feels a  flicker of malice  toward karuizawa  and adopts a new value system of saving the fifty within reach rather than aiming for a hundred  refuses to help her romantic rival and assures her nothing happened before the breakup  openly admits she likes him  walking to school together and meeting at the bench   a strong bond  reads her jealousy  refuses to help  and calmly asserts her own position","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p164-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p164-1\">Ichinose&#x27;s confrontation with Karuizawa; a new resolve<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.164–173<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Encounters Karuizawa on the way to school; reveals she knows her routine (7:50 AM) and that Ayanokōji waits on the bench to meet her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Popular? I&#x27;m just greeting my friends, like I did with you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Me? No way. There&#x27;s no way Ayanokouji-kun would date me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s really true. Ayanokouji-kun and I are not in that kind of relationship.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Perhaps he&#x27;s different from your average person. Is that what you wanted to say?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You know, don&#x27;t you, Karuizawa-san? That I like Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I guess I&#x27;m more about giving than receiving.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, I take back what I said earlier. Maybe I can&#x27;t help you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He&#x27;s waiting to meet with me at this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Kind but newly decisive — admits she likes Ayanokōji, feels a &quot;flicker of malice&quot; toward Karuizawa, and adopts a new value system of saving the fifty within reach rather than aiming for a hundred; refuses to help her romantic rival and assures her nothing happened before the breakup.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Openly admits she likes him; walking to school together and meeting at the bench; &quot;a strong bond.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Reads her jealousy, refuses to help, and calmly asserts her own position.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p90-1\">← Before: Ichinose&#x27;s gym meeting with Amasawa; deflecting the probe<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p184-1\">→ After: Class D&#x27;s victory; message to Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p180-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune class a s loss  horikita s regret  i m sorry  everyone  it s because i  couldn t do anything  class a loses to class d  koenji  who had a positive attitude toward written exams  is targeted with 25 penalty points   hirata suspects leaked information while karuizawa blames ayanokoji  racked with guilt and self loathing over the loss  apologizes to the class  hirata and karuizawa try to keep morale up by noting they haven t lost yet  he calmly urges the class to keep fighting and not lose motivation  she suspects ayanokoji leaked information about koenji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p180-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p180-1\">Class A&#x27;s loss; Horikita&#x27;s regret<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.180–183<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m sorry, everyone… It&#x27;s because I… couldn&#x27;t do anything…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Class A loses to Class D; Kōenji (who had a positive attitude toward written exams) is targeted with 25 penalty points — Hirata suspects leaked information while Karuizawa blames Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.180–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Racked with guilt and self-loathing over the loss, apologizes to the class; Hirata and Karuizawa try to keep morale up by noting they haven&#x27;t lost yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.180–183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He calmly urges the class to keep fighting and not lose motivation.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She suspects Ayanokōji leaked information about Kōenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p126-1\">← Before: The bench with Kushida; the collapse in her room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p203-1\">→ After: Alone in the dark: guilt, then Ibuki&#x27;s kick<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p184-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami class d s victory  message to ayanokoji  congratulations  everyone  we definitely had to defeat class a  and we did it splendidly  hoshinomiya s joy gives away class d s win before the results  class d beat class a  full class 2712 vs 2633  with well placed penalty points  including on hirata and kushida   1 25m pp split 40 ways  ayanokoji scored a perfect 100 despite receiving all 100 penalty points in his loss   getting a perfect score sure is amazing   it s thanks to your courage in choosing to trust in my advice that you won  the p 187 line is a phone message to ayanokoji  praising his perfect score  noting wasted penalty points  thanking him  and mentioning koenji s showing up and horikita s non participation  the p 188 line is his reply  overjoyed at defeating class a  humbled by ayanokoji s reply  and quietly credited by onlookers  kobashi iizuka  with having won over the mysterious boy  messages him  praising his perfect score and thanking him  he credits her courage in trusting his advice","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p184-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p184-1\">Class D&#x27;s victory; message to Ayanokōji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.184–188<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Congratulations, everyone. We definitely had to defeat Class A, and we did it splendidly!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Getting a perfect score sure is amazing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s thanks to your courage in choosing to trust in my advice that you won.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Hoshinomiya&#x27;s joy gives away Class D&#x27;s win before the results; Class D beat Class A (full-class 2712 vs 2633) with well-placed penalty points (including on Hirata and Kushida, ~1.25M PP split 40 ways); Ayanokōji scored a perfect 100 despite receiving all 100 penalty points in his loss.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The p.187 line is a phone message to Ayanokōji (praising his perfect score, noting wasted penalty points, thanking him, and mentioning Kōenji&#x27;s showing up and Horikita&#x27;s non-participation); the p.188 line is his reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Overjoyed at defeating Class A, humbled by Ayanokōji&#x27;s reply, and quietly credited by onlookers (Kobashi/Iizuka) with having won over the mysterious boy.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Messages him, praising his perfect score and thanking him; he credits her courage in trusting his advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v1-p164-1\">← Before: Ichinose&#x27;s confrontation with Karuizawa; a new resolve<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p189-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru shimazaki-ikkei hashimoto-masayoshi ichinose-honami morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the aftermath  shimazaki s challenge and ayanokoji s true plan  calm down  shimazaki  we won the exam  so it s all the same in the end   give me a break  ryuuen  i m busy today   the key to victory lies in the small group battles   what i really had to see through wasn t your irrational selection after you chose to abandon thinking  but the essence of the opponent your very aim   ryuuen  did this turn out the way you wanted it to   an alliance brings various benefits  his true aim wasn t penalty point accuracy but a demonstrative loss   taking all 100 penalty points and a perfect 100 score to show class c his ability and that ryuen feared him  predicted ryuen would abandon the academic fight and delay his leadership  and deliberately fed that via leaked  tasks  to the first year spies  coldly calculating   enters the small group battle assuming defeat because he  had to see through  ryuen s aim  not his lineup  turns the enemy s surveillance into a channel for his own message  ryuen barges in for a  winner s interview  ayanokoji reveals he read his intent and turned it against him  ryuen leaves  outmaneuvered  shimazaki confronts him over 0 5 penalty accuracy but ultimately acknowledges him  welcome to class c  they shake hands  he mediates  ayanokoji later explains the plan to him and morishita  reveals he had ichinose quietly gather intel on the first years  her cross class trust made her ideal  enabling the alliance s win  explains the plan  she had been skeptical about the first years being ryuen s spies","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p189-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p189-1\">The aftermath: Shimazaki&#x27;s challenge and Ayanokōji&#x27;s true plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.189–198<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Calm down, Shimazaki. We won the exam, so it&#x27;s all the same in the end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Give me a break, Ryuuen. I&#x27;m busy today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;The key to victory lies in the small-group battles.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What I really had to see through wasn&#x27;t your irrational selection after you chose to abandon thinking, but the essence of the opponent—your very aim.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ryuuen, did this turn out the way you wanted it to?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;An alliance brings various benefits.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> His true aim wasn&#x27;t penalty-point accuracy but a demonstrative loss — taking all 100 penalty points and a perfect 100 score to show Class C his ability and that Ryūen feared him; predicted Ryūen would abandon the academic fight and delay his leadership, and deliberately fed that via leaked &quot;tasks&quot; to the first-year spies.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coldly calculating — enters the small-group battle assuming defeat because he &quot;had to see through&quot; Ryūen&#x27;s aim, not his lineup; turns the enemy&#x27;s surveillance into a channel for his own message.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryūen barges in for a &quot;winner&#x27;s interview&quot;; Ayanokōji reveals he read his intent and turned it against him; Ryūen leaves, outmaneuvered.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Shimazaki confronts him over 0/5 penalty accuracy but ultimately acknowledges him (&quot;welcome to Class C&quot;); they shake hands.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> He mediates; Ayanokōji later explains the plan to him and Morishita.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Reveals he had Ichinose quietly gather intel on the first-years (her cross-class trust made her ideal), enabling the alliance&#x27;s win.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Explains the plan; she had been skeptical about the first-years being Ryūen&#x27;s spies.<span class=\"pg\">p.197–198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p156-1\">← Before: The eraser-crumb prank; Shiraishi signals the timing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p216-1\">→ After: After the welcome party; the dusk meeting with Kushida<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shimazaki-ikkei-y3v1-p189-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru shimazaki-ikkei","q":"shimazaki ikkei shimazaki confronts  then acknowledges ayanokoji  ayanokouji  you know what i want to say  right   you missed every single participant  you really made a remarkable debut   i told you  this special exam was supposed to be an easy win   then i won t be holding back  ayanokouji   honestly  you re far more amazing than i imagined  no wonder hashimoto relies on you   ayanokouji  welcome to class c  stern and academically proud   confronts ayanokoji over his  disastrous  0 5 prediction  but after ayanokoji explains his true intent and shows a perfect 100 score  far above other a rated students  shifts from anger to genuine acknowledgment and welcomes him  challenges him  then accepts him as class c s leader  defies ryuen s mocking by praising ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shimazaki-ikkei-y3v1-p189-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shimazaki-ikkei.html#sc-shimazaki-ikkei-y3v1-p189-1\">Shimazaki confronts, then acknowledges Ayanokōji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.189–198<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji. You know what I want to say, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> &quot;You missed every single participant. You really made a remarkable debut.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> &quot;I told you, this special exam was supposed to be an easy win.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then I won&#x27;t be holding back, Ayanokouji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Honestly, you&#x27;re far more amazing than I imagined. No wonder Hashimoto relies on you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji… welcome to Class C.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Stern and academically proud — confronts Ayanokōji over his &quot;disastrous&quot; 0/5 prediction, but after Ayanokōji explains his true intent and shows a perfect 100 score (far above other A-rated students), shifts from anger to genuine acknowledgment and welcomes him.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Challenges him, then accepts him as Class C&#x27;s leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Defies Ryūen&#x27;s mocking by praising Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p190-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ryuen s  winner s interview  and defeat  yo  don t mind me   i came all the way here for a winner s interview  move it   so  has it been officially decided that you ll lead class c from now on  ayanokouji   kukuku  i see  it does seem like you re busy   that s how it is  huh  bring it on  barges into class c to gloat and confirm ayanokoji wasn t recognized as leader   but is outmaneuvered  his 100 point penalty and strategy of abandoning the academic fight were read and turned into ayanokoji s proof of strength  leaves in miserable retreat  tried to delay his leadership  gives him all 100 penalty points out of caution  which backfires into ayanokoji s demonstration  ibuki covers ishizaki s mouth as he tries to speak to ryuen after","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p190-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p190-1\">Ryūen&#x27;s &quot;winner&#x27;s interview&quot; and defeat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.190–197<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Yo, don&#x27;t mind me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;I came all the way here for a winner&#x27;s interview, move it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;So? Has it been officially decided that you&#x27;ll lead Class C from now on, Ayanokouji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Kukuku. I see, it does seem like you&#x27;re busy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s how it is, huh…? Bring it on.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Barges into Class C to gloat and confirm Ayanokōji wasn&#x27;t recognized as leader — but is outmaneuvered: his 100-point penalty and strategy of abandoning the academic fight were read and turned into Ayanokōji&#x27;s proof of strength; leaves in miserable retreat.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Tried to delay his leadership; gives him all 100 penalty points out of caution, which backfires into Ayanokōji&#x27;s demonstration.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Ibuki covers Ishizaki&#x27;s mouth as he tries to speak to Ryūen after.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v1-p142-1\">← Before: Horikita&#x27;s state discussed; info-leak precautions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p203-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune alone in the dark  guilt  then ibuki s kick stays alone in class a s empty classroom after the loss  blaming herself for failing to devise even one strategy in the wake of ayanokoji s transfer   i should go home  no one blamed her   they comforted her saying there d be a next time  but their warm words hardly registered  she sat mind void until she was the last one left  the classroom dyed in twilight  walks the deserted corridor in a loop of self doubt  i m becoming useless  then outside onto gravel   and is suddenly kicked in the back without warning  thrown forward  hands and knees stinging  bag rolling away in dust   what  what was that   what are you doing  you re out of your mind   i don t understand what you mean  paralyzed by guilt and loneliness  unable to recover  even when kicked she can t retaliate  noting small amounts of blood seeping into her palm  kicks her from behind with full force  calls her pathetic  and says her spineless appearance irritates her  leaves after venting","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p203-1\">Alone in the dark: guilt, then Ibuki&#x27;s kick<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.203–209<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stays alone in Class A&#x27;s empty classroom after the loss, blaming herself for failing to devise even one strategy in the wake of Ayanokōji&#x27;s transfer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I should go home…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;What… What was that!?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;What are you doing…? You&#x27;re out of your mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> No one blamed her — they comforted her saying there&#x27;d be a next time, but their warm words hardly registered; she sat mind-void until she was the last one left, the classroom dyed in twilight.<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Walks the deserted corridor in a loop of self-doubt (&quot;I&#x27;m becoming useless&quot;), then outside onto gravel — and is suddenly kicked in the back without warning, thrown forward, hands and knees stinging, bag rolling away in dust.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t understand what you mean.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Paralyzed by guilt and loneliness, unable to recover; even when kicked she can&#x27;t retaliate, noting small amounts of blood seeping into her palm.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Kicks her from behind with full force, calls her pathetic, and says her spineless appearance irritates her; leaves after venting.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p180-1\">← Before: Class A&#x27;s loss; Horikita&#x27;s regret<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p209-1\">→ After: The bench with Karuizawa: a heart-to-heart<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p207-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki kicks horikita out of frustration finds horikita walking alone on the gravel outside the dorm after the exam and kicks her hard in the back without warning   you ve grown pathetic  horikita  you can t even dodge a kick like that   your pathetic appearance has always been irritating to me  it pisses me off just looking at you   see  that s what i mean  that kind of spineless attitude keeps jumping into my line of sight  it can t be helped  you should be thankful i only kicked you   everyone s always going off about ayanokouji this  ayanokouji that  can t you be glad that the plague is finally gone from your class   i d jump for joy  just seeing his face makes me so angry  ah  just thinking about it makes me angry   if you plan to stay this pathetic forever  i m done with you  don t ever get involved with me again  in fact  don t even come into my sight  combative and foul tempered   kicks a defenseless horikita in frustration  insists it had not one percent of malice  vents that ayanokoji s departure should be celebrated but it was ryuen who got embarrassed  and storms off  she had been lingering by the bench as if waiting for someone   possibly worried about horikita in her own rough way  though horikita dismisses the notion  kicks her  calls her pathetic  and orders her to stay out of her sight  she had helped ibuki when she was short on cash but was never thanked  enraged at the mere thought of him  claims she d  jump for joy  at his leaving  bitter that it was ryuen  not ayanokoji  who ended up embarrassed in the exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p207-1\">Ibuki kicks Horikita out of frustration<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.207–208<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Finds Horikita walking alone on the gravel outside the dorm after the exam and kicks her hard in the back without warning.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;ve grown pathetic, Horikita. You can&#x27;t even dodge a kick like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;Your pathetic appearance has always been irritating to me. It pisses me off just looking at you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;See, that&#x27;s what I mean. That kind of spineless attitude keeps jumping into my line of sight; it can&#x27;t be helped. You should be thankful I only kicked you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Everyone&#x27;s always going off about Ayanokouji this, Ayanokouji that. Can&#x27;t you be glad that the plague is finally gone from your class?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;d jump for joy. Just seeing his face makes me so angry… Ah, just thinking about it makes me angry.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you plan to stay this pathetic forever, I&#x27;m done with you. Don&#x27;t ever get involved with me again, in fact, don&#x27;t even come into my sight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Combative and foul-tempered — kicks a defenseless Horikita in frustration, insists it had not one percent of malice, vents that Ayanokōji&#x27;s departure should be celebrated but it was Ryūen who got embarrassed, and storms off.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> She had been lingering by the bench as if waiting for someone — possibly worried about Horikita in her own rough way, though Horikita dismisses the notion.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Kicks her, calls her pathetic, and orders her to stay out of her sight; she had helped Ibuki when she was short on cash but was never thanked.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Enraged at the mere thought of him; claims she&#x27;d &quot;jump for joy&quot; at his leaving.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Bitter that it was Ryūen, not Ayanokōji, who ended up embarrassed in the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p136-1\">← Before: Ibuki&#x27;s disdain and Horikita&#x27;s cooking<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p257-1\">→ After: &quot;Behind the Scenes, Part 1&quot;: resisting the comfort of Horikita&#x27;s room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p209-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"karuizawa-kei ibuki-mio ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the bench with karuizawa  a heart to heart crouches on the ground in pain when karuizawa  still in uniform  comes over from a nearby bench  concerned  and offers to call a teacher   i m fine  the pain is finally starting to subside  she really has no common sense   i m really hopeless right now   i m sorry about today s exam as well  i couldn t lead the class to victory   it s not true  i thought i was quite strong myself  but it wasn t me who was strong   i realized that it was only because ayanokouji kun was in the class that i was able to stand up straight   what kind of person was ayanokouji kun to you   do you  like ayanokouji kun too   i  haven t been taught anything by him   i m pathetic  aren t i   now that it s come to this  i have no choice but to make him turn his head this way  and i will graduate with everyone in class a  i promise   not at all  i m a weak person  but i ve realized that i m not alone   yes let s definitely make him regret it  karuizawa gently grabs her wrist to help her up  her palm bloodied and dirty  and brushes dirt off her uniform with a handkerchief  the hand that should have hurt forgot its pain  karuizawa reveals ayanokoji was  someone i love  refuses to say whether the transfer was his idea  not saying it  that s become my reason for existence  and tells her the secret of her first year   middle school bullying  climbing the social hierarchy  fake romance with hirata  the renewal of bullying and her rescue  itself orchestrated  and the rooftop battle with ryuen  karuizawa s question makes her recall spring break   a pleasant  embarrassing pounding in her chest she can t deny  she realizes she was left out  having known only ayanokoji s back  and cries at the unfairness of it all  breaks down  then slowly recovers   realizing she must make ayanokoji  turn his head this way  and graduate from class a with everyone  for the first time takes a step forward in reality and in her heart  the two bond over being  involved with a really difficult person  karuizawa shares her painful past  and they resolve together to make ayanokoji regret transferring out  considers that ibuki might have been worried in her own way  she had been lingering by the bench as if waiting for someone  realizes he never turned around or waited for her  that she knew him less than anyone  resolves to make him look back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p209-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p209-1\">The bench with Karuizawa: a heart-to-heart<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.209–215<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Crouches on the ground in pain when Karuizawa, still in uniform, comes over from a nearby bench, concerned, and offers to call a teacher.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m fine… the pain is finally starting to subside. She really has no common sense…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m really hopeless right now…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m sorry about today&#x27;s exam as well. I couldn&#x27;t lead the class to victory.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s not true. I thought I was quite strong myself, but it wasn&#x27;t me who was strong…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I realized that it was only because Ayanokouji-kun was in the class that I was able to stand up straight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;What kind of person was Ayanokouji-kun to you…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Do you… like Ayanokouji-kun too?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I… haven&#x27;t been taught anything by him…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m pathetic, aren&#x27;t I…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Now that it&#x27;s come to this, I have no choice but to make him turn his head this way. And I will graduate with everyone in Class A. I promise.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Not at all. I&#x27;m a weak person, but I&#x27;ve realized that I&#x27;m not alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Yes—let&#x27;s definitely make him regret it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Karuizawa gently grabs her wrist to help her up (her palm bloodied and dirty) and brushes dirt off her uniform with a handkerchief; the hand that should have hurt forgot its pain.<span class=\"pg\">p.209–210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Karuizawa reveals Ayanokōji was &quot;someone I love,&quot; refuses to say whether the transfer was his idea (&quot;Not saying it… that&#x27;s become my reason for existence&quot;), and tells her the secret of her first year — middle-school bullying, climbing the social hierarchy, fake romance with Hirata, the renewal of bullying and her rescue (itself orchestrated), and the rooftop battle with Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.211–213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Karuizawa&#x27;s question makes her recall spring break — a pleasant, embarrassing pounding in her chest she can&#x27;t deny; she realizes she was left out, having known only Ayanokōji&#x27;s back, and cries at the unfairness of it all.<span class=\"pg\">p.212–215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Breaks down, then slowly recovers — realizing she must make Ayanokōji &quot;turn his head this way&quot; and graduate from Class A with everyone; for the first time takes a step forward in reality and in her heart.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The two bond over being &quot;involved with a really difficult person&quot;; Karuizawa shares her painful past, and they resolve together to make Ayanokōji regret transferring out.<span class=\"pg\">p.209–215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Considers that Ibuki might have been worried in her own way; she had been lingering by the bench as if waiting for someone.<span class=\"pg\">p.211–212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Realizes he never turned around or waited for her, that she knew him less than anyone; resolves to make him look back.<span class=\"pg\">p.210–215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v1-p203-1\">← Before: Alone in the dark: guilt, then Ibuki&#x27;s kick<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p209-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka hasebe-haruka hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei karuizawa finds horikita  sharing her painful past still in uniform  sees ibuki kick horikita from a nearby bench  comes over and gently helps the bloodied  dirtied girl up  brushing dirt from her uniform with a handkerchief   are you okay   it looked like she hit your back really hard  are you hurt  should i call a teacher   i don t think it s your fault  if we had scored more points  we could ve won the full class battle   that s not true  you ve had a distinct backbone from the moment you entered school   he s a crucial person to me  someone important  someone i love   i can t say  not saying it  that s become my reason for existence   do you  like ayanokouji kun too   but you couldn t respond right away  isn t that telling   kiyotaka no  ayanokouji kun  he saved me from the darkness   i ll tell only you  horikita san  the secret i have with ayanokouji kun  even maya chan doesn t know   i feel the same way   we both got involved with a really difficult person  didn t we   you really are strong  horikita san   let s make him regret transferring out of our class  reveals her first year secret  middle school bullying  resolving to climb the school s social hierarchy even if disliked  the fake romance with hirata  the new wave of bullying when the truth emerged  her rescue through ayanokoji s intervention  itself orchestrated  and the rooftop battle with ryuen   details ibuki s account had lacked  kind and emotionally open   tends to horikita s wounds  shares her vulnerable past and feelings for ayanokoji  and resolves to change her mindset and make him regret leaving class a  her  natural smile  is something horikita had not seen since the breakup  helps her up  confides in her  and bonds over their shared feelings   feeling more connected to her than anyone else in the class  still loves him  refuses to say whether the transfer was his idea  calls him the one who saved her from darkness  and vows to make him regret leaving  refers to her as  maya chan    her close friend who doesn t know her secret  the fake romance in her first year","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p209-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p209-1\">Karuizawa finds Horikita; sharing her painful past<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.209–215<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still in uniform, sees Ibuki kick Horikita from a nearby bench, comes over and gently helps the bloodied, dirtied girl up, brushing dirt from her uniform with a handkerchief.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;Are you okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;It looked like she hit your back really hard, are you hurt? Should I call a teacher?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t think it&#x27;s your fault. If we had scored more points, we could&#x27;ve won the full-class battle.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s not true. You&#x27;ve had a distinct backbone from the moment you entered school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He&#x27;s a crucial person to me. Someone important… someone I love…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can&#x27;t say. Not saying it… that&#x27;s become my reason for existence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you… like Ayanokouji-kun too?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But you couldn&#x27;t respond right away, isn&#x27;t that telling?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Kiyotaka—no, Ayanokouji-kun… he saved me from the darkness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll tell only you, Horikita-san, the secret I have with Ayanokouji-kun. Even Maya-chan doesn&#x27;t know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I feel the same way.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We both got involved with a really difficult person, didn&#x27;t we?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You really are strong, Horikita-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s make him regret transferring out of our class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Reveals her first-year secret: middle-school bullying, resolving to climb the school&#x27;s social hierarchy even if disliked, the fake romance with Hirata, the new wave of bullying when the truth emerged, her rescue through Ayanokōji&#x27;s intervention (itself orchestrated), and the rooftop battle with Ryūen — details Ibuki&#x27;s account had lacked.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Kind and emotionally open — tends to Horikita&#x27;s wounds, shares her vulnerable past and feelings for Ayanokōji, and resolves to change her mindset and make him regret leaving Class A; her &quot;natural smile&quot; is something Horikita had not seen since the breakup.<span class=\"pg\">p.209–215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Helps her up, confides in her, and bonds over their shared feelings — feeling more connected to her than anyone else in the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.209–215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Still loves him; refuses to say whether the transfer was his idea, calls him the one who saved her from darkness, and vows to make him regret leaving.<span class=\"pg\">p.211–215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Refers to her as &quot;Maya-chan&quot; — her close friend who doesn&#x27;t know her secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The fake romance in her first year.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p163-1\">← Before: Karuizawa&#x27;s heartbreak; confronting Ichinose about Ayanokōji<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p271-1\">→ After: &quot;Mock Date&quot;: a secret date at Keyaki Mall<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p216-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka after the welcome party  the dusk meeting with kushida returns from a small class c welcome party at keyaki mall  takes a detour from the dorm route  and meets kushida   whom he called out   waiting at the railing at dusk   why did you choose this place to meet   that did happen   it was something like an accident  but i was really anxious when you threatened me    kushida reflects that for third years there is no time to rest   it is  already april  and preparation for career choices and the next exam is like stocking emergency supplies before a catastrophe  deliberately chose an isolated spot  echoing where kushida once offered her body to keep him silent  notes her true nature was revealed to class a but not widely known elsewhere  called her out to a secluded dusk meeting  she evades his question about the place  guarded after their first year transaction","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p216-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p216-1\">After the welcome party; the dusk meeting with Kushida<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.216–220<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns from a small Class C welcome party at Keyaki Mall, takes a detour from the dorm route, and meets Kushida — whom he called out — waiting at the railing at dusk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Why did you choose this place to meet?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;That did happen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;It was something like an accident, but I was really anxious when you threatened me.&quot; — Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Reflects that for third-years there is no time to rest — it is &quot;already April,&quot; and preparation for career choices and the next exam is like stocking emergency supplies before a catastrophe.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately chose an isolated spot (echoing where Kushida once offered her body to keep him silent); notes her true nature was revealed to Class A but not widely known elsewhere.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Called her out to a secluded dusk meeting; she evades his question about the place, guarded after their first-year transaction.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p189-1\">← Before: The aftermath: Shimazaki&#x27;s challenge and Ayanokōji&#x27;s true plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p220-1\">→ After: Recruiting Kushida as an insider; subtle threats<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p216-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo kushida s dusk meeting  ayanokoji s offer of betrayal waits alone leaning on the railing at dusk  having been called out by ayanokoji  refuses to turn around at first   when we first entered school  you saw quite a lot of things you shouldn t have  ayanokouji kun   it was something like an accident  but i was really anxious when you threatened me   really  you ve been thinking about setting me up since then  haven t you   i have no such intentions  really   what  are you seriously asking me to betray my class   because of our previous private point transaction  i ended up in trouble  do you think i would cooperate with you again now that you ve become an enemy   do you think that counts as a threat  ryuuen kun knows about it too   you don t even need my strength to take down horikita s pathetic class   huh  you sure think highly of her  don t you   expulsions  from our class   that s  like  really risky  even if i get a little allowance on the side and drag down the class  it s meaningless if i can t graduate from class a   how serious are you   what s that about  so what do you want  ayanokouji kun  you want to bring down class a  right   i don t really get it  but it seems like you just want things to go your way  guarded and two faced   evades his questions  notes she was anxious when he threatened her two years ago  refuses the betrayal offer citing their last transaction s trouble  yet never turns to face him and masks her true intentions  her   superficial skepticism  hides genuine calculation  is recruited as an insider  rejects the offer on the surface but leaves the door open  unable to read whether he is bluffing  disparages her as  pathetic  and is surprised ayanokoji thinks highly of her  her reunion with her same middle school kouhai caused her past stress  points out he also knows her secret  but his rumors would lack credibility","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p216-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p216-1\">Kushida&#x27;s dusk meeting: Ayanokōji&#x27;s offer of betrayal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.216–223<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits alone leaning on the railing at dusk, having been called out by Ayanokōji; refuses to turn around at first.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;When we first entered school, you saw quite a lot of things you shouldn&#x27;t have, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;It was something like an accident, but I was really anxious when you threatened me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Really? You&#x27;ve been thinking about setting me up since then, haven&#x27;t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have no such intentions. Really.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What? Are you seriously asking me to betray my class?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Because of our previous Private Point transaction, I ended up in trouble. Do you think I would cooperate with you again now that you&#x27;ve become an enemy?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you think that counts as a threat? Ryuuen-kun knows about it too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You don&#x27;t even need my strength to take down Horikita&#x27;s pathetic class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Huh? You sure think highly of her, don&#x27;t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Expulsions… from our class?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s, like, really risky. Even if I get a little allowance on the side and drag down the class, it&#x27;s meaningless if I can&#x27;t graduate from Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;How serious are you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What&#x27;s that about? So what do you want, Ayanokouji-kun? You want to bring down Class A, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t really get it, but it seems like you just want things to go your way.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Guarded and two-faced — evades his questions, notes she was anxious when he threatened her two years ago, refuses the betrayal offer citing their last transaction&#x27;s trouble, yet never turns to face him and masks her true intentions; her &quot; superficial skepticism&quot; hides genuine calculation.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is recruited as an insider; rejects the offer on the surface but leaves the door open, unable to read whether he is bluffing.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Disparages her as &quot;pathetic&quot; and is surprised Ayanokōji thinks highly of her; her reunion with her same-middle-school kouhai caused her past stress.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Points out he also knows her secret, but his rumors would lack credibility.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y3v1-p126-1\">← Before: Kushida needles the gloomy Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p220-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune ichinose-honami shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka recruiting kushida as an insider  subtle threats  i was just wondering how the class is doing  i m a bit worried   to close the gap we have with class a  it would be easier to have an insider from now on   that s exactly it  if you deliver results  i ll pay you in private points   you re free not to cooperate  but in that case  i can t guarantee i ll keep your secrets   it won t be that easy  horikita will definitely recover soon   besides  if we need to forcibly expel some people in the future  that would change things   then you ll have to save up enough private points to transfer in the remaining year   i m not asking for an immediate answer  you re free to tell horikita or anyone else about this invitation to betrayal   unfortunately  i want more than just one thing  uses her exposed secret as leverage  her nature known to class a but not other classes  ryuen s rumors would lack credibility  hints at future expulsions from class a  giving her an incentive to save transfer money  and lets her record the whole thing to strengthen class a s unity if she wishes   a calculated  multi layered gambit  calm and manipulative   makes an open offer of betrayal backed by veiled blackmail  refuses to over explain  and deliberately leaves her room to maneuver  notes she is masking her true intentions as much as he is  offers to pay her for class a intel  implicitly threatens to expose her secret and hints at expelling her classmates  expects her to recover soon and become a significant obstacle  has no intention of recruiting her while she leads  discusses how he advised her class   yukimura  hirata and wan mei yui s roles  and koenji as the exploitable opportunity  credits ichinose s own intel gathering as the reason she could accept his advice  reminisces about a white room dropout girl he met once before enrolling   a memory he has almost entirely forgotten  99  of it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p220-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p220-1\">Recruiting Kushida as an insider; subtle threats<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.220–223<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I was just wondering how the class is doing. I&#x27;m a bit worried.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;To close the gap we have with Class A, it would be easier to have an insider from now on.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;That&#x27;s exactly it. If you deliver results, I&#x27;ll pay you in private points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re free not to cooperate, but in that case, I can&#x27;t guarantee I&#x27;ll keep your secrets.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It won&#x27;t be that easy. Horikita will definitely recover soon.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Besides, if we need to forcibly expel some people in the future, that would change things.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then you&#x27;ll have to save up enough Private Points to transfer in the remaining year.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m not asking for an immediate answer. You&#x27;re free to tell Horikita or anyone else about this invitation to betrayal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Unfortunately, I want more than just one thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Uses her exposed secret as leverage (her nature known to Class A but not other classes; Ryūen&#x27;s rumors would lack credibility); hints at future expulsions from Class A, giving her an incentive to save transfer money, and lets her record the whole thing to strengthen Class A&#x27;s unity if she wishes — a calculated, multi-layered gambit.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and manipulative — makes an open offer of betrayal backed by veiled blackmail, refuses to over-explain, and deliberately leaves her room to maneuver; notes she is masking her true intentions as much as he is.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Offers to pay her for Class A intel; implicitly threatens to expose her secret and hints at expelling her classmates.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Expects her to recover soon and become a significant obstacle; has no intention of recruiting her while she leads.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Discusses how he advised her class — Yukimura, Hirata and Wan Mei-Yui&#x27;s roles, and Kōenji as the exploitable opportunity; credits Ichinose&#x27;s own intel gathering as the reason she could accept his advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Reminisces about a White Room dropout girl he met once before enrolling — a memory he has almost entirely forgotten (&quot;99% of it&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p216-1\">← Before: After the welcome party; the dusk meeting with Kushida<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-1\">→ After: Meeting Tsubaki and Utomiya; remembering Yuki<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"tsubaki-sakurako utomiya-riku yuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka meeting tsubaki and utomiya  remembering yuki leaves school after class and runs into utomiya and tsubaki on the way to the dorm  they mention the rumor about his transfer   it feels like it s been a while since i ve seen the two of you together   we re not together all the time    tsubaki  tsubaki sakurako  huh   what is it  it s creepy when you suddenly call me by my full name   recently  i suddenly thought of someone other than my family that i d like to meet   how should i put this  if i had to put it in familiar terms  they would probably be a childhood friend  i guess  tsubaki s name and her training camp question  do you like snow   snow   yuki  trigger a faint memory of a white room girl named yuki  the snow camellia  yuki tsubaki  connection makes him wonder whether it was really coincidence  finds himself recalling  unnecessary memories  of the white room  concludes it would be better not to actually meet yuki again  since the past and present would likely be unchanged  meets her and utomiya  calling her by her full name startles her  she presses him about the person he d like to meet  he greets him reluctantly  utomiya sharply interjects when tsubaki s conversation turns personal  remembered as a white room classmate   the only girl he studied with there","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-1\">Meeting Tsubaki and Utomiya; remembering Yuki<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.225–228<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaves school after class and runs into Utomiya and Tsubaki on the way to the dorm; they mention the rumor about his transfer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yuki\">Yuki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;It feels like it&#x27;s been a while since I&#x27;ve seen the two of you together.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;We&#x27;re not together all the time.&quot; — Tsubaki<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Tsubaki Sakurako… huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What is it? It&#x27;s creepy when you suddenly call me by my full name.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Recently, I suddenly thought of someone other than my family that I&#x27;d like to meet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;How should I put this? If I had to put it in familiar terms, they would probably be a childhood friend… I guess.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Tsubaki&#x27;s name and her training-camp question &quot;do you like snow?&quot; (snow = yuki) trigger a faint memory of a White Room girl named Yuki; the snow camellia (yuki-tsubaki) connection makes him wonder whether it was really coincidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.226–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Finds himself recalling &quot;unnecessary memories&quot; of the White Room; concludes it would be better not to actually meet Yuki again, since the past and present would likely be unchanged.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> Meets her and Utomiya; calling her by her full name startles her; she presses him about the person he&#x27;d like to meet.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> He greets him reluctantly; Utomiya sharply interjects when Tsubaki&#x27;s conversation turns personal.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yuki<\/b> Remembered as a White Room classmate — the only girl he studied with there.<span class=\"pg\">p.227–228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p220-1\">← Before: Recruiting Kushida as an insider; subtle threats<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p229-1\">→ After: Kitou&#x27;s challenge: a show of strength behind the dorm<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p229-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"kitou-hayato ryuuen-kakeru sawada sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kitou s challenge  a show of strength behind the dorm meets kitou hayato  who called him to a spot near the garbage disposal area behind the dorm  kitou refuses to recognize him as leader   good  you didn t run away    kitou  i don t recognize you as a leader    kitou  you can t bring yourself to recognize anyone other than sakayanagi  can you   as long as i m not the person leading the class  someone needs to step forward    kitou  you re the same as sakayanagi  you don t really care about graduating from class a    kitou  i don t trust you    kitou  show me that you can suppress my dissatisfaction with your strength    kitou  if you had acted fast enough  you could ve prevented sawada from getting into danger   ugh    kitou  you re strong  is there this much of a difference    kitou  i ll look forward to that  accepts kitou s physical challenge on his terms   dodges punches and kicks  lands one left fist blow to the abdomen and slaps both ears to break his guard  then offers respect and a promise to raise class c  winning him over  tests him  refuses to follow until bested  then takes his hand and pledges loyalty  compares kitou s fighting style to ryuen s   kitou s upper body more refined  legs less so  rebukes kitou for not acting when she was endangered during ryuen s classroom intrusion  kitou had followed her believing she had the higher chance of winning","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p229-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p229-1\">Kitou&#x27;s challenge: a show of strength behind the dorm<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.229–234<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Kitou Hayato, who called him to a spot near the garbage disposal area behind the dorm; Kitou refuses to recognize him as leader.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Good, you didn&#x27;t run away.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t recognize you as a leader.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;You can&#x27;t bring yourself to recognize anyone other than Sakayanagi, can you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;As long as I&#x27;m not the person leading the class, someone needs to step forward.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re the same as Sakayanagi. You don&#x27;t really care about graduating from Class A.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t trust you.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Show me that you can suppress my dissatisfaction with your strength.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;if you had acted fast enough, you could&#x27;ve prevented Sawada from getting into danger.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ugh…!&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re strong… Is there this much of a difference…?&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll look forward to that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Accepts Kitou&#x27;s physical challenge on his terms — dodges punches and kicks, lands one left-fist blow to the abdomen and slaps both ears to break his guard; then offers respect and a promise to raise Class C, winning him over.<span class=\"pg\">p.229–234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Tests him; refuses to follow until bested, then takes his hand and pledges loyalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.229–234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Compares Kitou&#x27;s fighting style to Ryūen&#x27;s — Kitou&#x27;s upper body more refined, legs less so.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">sawada<\/b> Rebukes Kitou for not acting when she was endangered during Ryūen&#x27;s classroom intrusion.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Kitou had followed her believing she had the higher chance of winning.<span class=\"pg\">p.229–230<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-1\">← Before: Meeting Tsubaki and Utomiya; remembering Yuki<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p236-1\">→ After: Closing the distance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p236-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka closing the distance reflects that he must close the distance with each student in the way most suitable to them   a conversation for those who seek it  a show of strength for those who seek it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p236-1\">Closing the distance<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.236<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reflects that he must close the distance with each student in the way most suitable to them — a conversation for those who seek it, a show of strength for those who seek it.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p229-1\">← Before: Kitou&#x27;s challenge: a show of strength behind the dorm<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p257-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio  behind the scenes  part 1  resisting the comfort of horikita s room flops on the floor of horikita s room  staring at the ceiling  resolving that she should stop coming for the free meals before she grows too close   if it weren t for the free meals  i wouldn t have come to a place like this  secretly admits she has come to see horikita and kushida s room as a  comfortable space  and that she is getting closer to people she detests  decides to distance herself   until the smell of food makes her forget the resolve  enjoys her cooking but tells herself she should leave before growing attached  also growing closer to her despite detesting her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p257-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p257-1\">&quot;Behind the Scenes, Part 1&quot;: resisting the comfort of Horikita&#x27;s room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.257<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Flops on the floor of Horikita&#x27;s room, staring at the ceiling, resolving that she should stop coming for the free meals before she grows too close.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;If it weren&#x27;t for the free meals, I wouldn&#x27;t have come to a place like this…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Secretly admits she has come to see Horikita and Kushida&#x27;s room as a &quot;comfortable space&quot; and that she is getting closer to people she detests; decides to distance herself — until the smell of food makes her forget the resolve.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Enjoys her cooking but tells herself she should leave before growing attached.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Also growing closer to her despite detesting her.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p207-1\">← Before: Ibuki kicks Horikita out of frustration<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p265-1\">→ After: &quot;Concern?&quot;: the impulse behind the kick<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p261-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka morishita-ai","q":"morishita ai  gatling gun  the eraser shaving battlefield  this would be a life or death battle  i firmly resolved myself for this   fire   looking behind you during class  even during the self study period  is something only a naughty  naughty student would do  please face forward and focus on what you have to do   staring at my face from such a close distance  what a pervert   not at all  i m seriously engaged in the class  frames flicking eraser shavings at ayanokoji s head as a  gatling gun  assault by a commander against an  evil titan  fires a single  bullet  then a rapid volley  and when caught diverts attention with the  pervert  line   all in playful  melodramatic combat language  her  target  the  evil titan  notes a second enemy  shiraishi  is also present","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p261-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html#sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p261-1\">&quot;Gatling Gun&quot;: the eraser-shaving battlefield<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.261–262<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;THIS WOULD BE a life-or-death battle. I firmly resolved myself for this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;Fire—!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;Looking behind you during class, even during the self-study period, is something only a naughty, naughty student would do. Please face forward and focus on what you have to do.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Staring at my face from such a close distance, what a pervert.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Not at all? I&#x27;m seriously engaged in the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Frames flicking eraser shavings at Ayanokōji&#x27;s head as a &quot;Gatling gun&quot; assault by a commander against an &quot;evil titan&quot;; fires a single &quot;bullet&quot; then a rapid volley, and when caught diverts attention with the &quot;pervert&quot; line — all in playful, melodramatic combat language.<span class=\"pg\">p.261–262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her &quot;target,&quot; the &quot;evil titan&quot;; notes a second enemy (Shiraishi) is also present.<span class=\"pg\">p.261–262<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-morishita-ai-y3v1-p146-1\">← Before: Morishita&#x27;s eraser-crumb prank and &quot;Jeanne d&#x27;Arc&quot; defense<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p265-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio  concern  the impulse behind the kick paces near the school entrance after school  waiting for horikita  irritated that the free meals have stopped and that horikita has been dejected since ayanokoji s transfer   come out already  how concerned do you plan to make  no  no  i m not concerned  cannot admit she is worried   pushes the feeling away as odd thinking from not having eaten well  recalls katsuragi s advice that a person should only be kicked if they would benefit from it  and acts on impulse when horikita emerges lifeless  waits over half an hour for her  then delivers the  merciless kick  in ch 8   framed here as a rough attempt to snap her out of her depression and get meals again  recalls his words about when it is permissible to kick someone  secretly pleased at his transfer and at ryuen s strategy being seen through  but the greater frustration is horikita s state","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p265-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p265-1\">&quot;Concern?&quot;: the impulse behind the kick<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.265–266<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Paces near the school entrance after school, waiting for Horikita, irritated that the free meals have stopped and that Horikita has been dejected since Ayanokōji&#x27;s transfer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;Come out already. How concerned do you plan to make… no, no, I&#x27;m not concerned.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cannot admit she is worried — pushes the feeling away as odd thinking from not having eaten well; recalls Katsuragi&#x27;s advice that a person should only be kicked if they would benefit from it, and acts on impulse when Horikita emerges lifeless.<span class=\"pg\">p.265–266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Waits over half an hour for her, then delivers the &quot;merciless kick&quot; in Ch.8 — framed here as a rough attempt to snap her out of her depression and get meals again.<span class=\"pg\">p.265–266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Recalls his words about when it is permissible to kick someone.<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Secretly pleased at his transfer and at Ryūen&#x27;s strategy being seen through, but the greater frustration is Horikita&#x27;s state.<span class=\"pg\">p.265<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p257-1\">← Before: &quot;Behind the Scenes, Part 1&quot;: resisting the comfort of Horikita&#x27;s room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hasebe-haruka-y3v1-p267-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka hasebe-haruka","q":"hasebe haruka  a pillar of support  watching sakura on tv sits before her computer at 1 a m  thursday  waiting for the online show  idol in the making  to broadcast  thinking about ayanokoji s transfer   my fault   how arrogant of me  right   is it okay if i talk a little   yeah  that s right  he transferred   keep going   i ll also work hard for one more year  so you won t laugh at me when we finally meet on the outside  okay   keep going  airi  guilt ridden over having resented ayanokoji for sakura s expulsion  she resolves to keep cheering her friend on from afar   realizing sakura has  started walking forward  while she was left behind  and vowing to work hard for one more year so they can meet again outside the school  sakura  now idol  9 on the show  she watches her confess a crush from her first year and keeps cheering her on  blames herself for his transfer  then concludes he must have had reasons beyond her understanding","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y3v1-p267-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html#sc-hasebe-haruka-y3v1-p267-1\">&quot;A Pillar of Support&quot;: watching Sakura on TV<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.267–270<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits before her computer at 1 a.m. Thursday, waiting for the online show &quot;Idol in the Making&quot; to broadcast, thinking about Ayanokōji&#x27;s transfer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> &quot;…My fault?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> &quot;How arrogant of me, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> &quot;Is it okay if I talk a little?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Yeah, that&#x27;s right. He transferred.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Keep going…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll also work hard for one more year… so you won&#x27;t laugh at me when we finally meet on the outside, okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Keep going, Airi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Guilt-ridden over having resented Ayanokōji for Sakura&#x27;s expulsion, she resolves to keep cheering her friend on from afar — realizing Sakura has &quot;started walking forward&quot; while she was left behind, and vowing to work hard for one more year so they can meet again outside the school.<span class=\"pg\">p.267–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Sakura, now idol #9 on the show; she watches her confess a crush from her first year and keeps cheering her on.<span class=\"pg\">p.267–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Blames herself for his transfer, then concludes he must have had reasons beyond her understanding.<span class=\"pg\">p.267–269<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p271-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei  mock date  a secret date at keyaki mall goes alone to keyaki mall before the island exam to try a  mock date  with ayanokoji   arriving separately and messaging each other while browsing the stores   phew  i m kind of nervous   this is cute   it s almost as if he stepped out of a manga   he really is simple minded  playful and affectionate   enjoys the secret text message date  teases his  terrible taste  in a skull strap  and wants to date him  openly and proudly  as soon as possible  touched that he silently left the kitten strap she liked at her door  her boyfriend  they hold a secret mock date via messages  and he later leaves the kitten phone strap at her door","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p271-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p271-1\">&quot;Mock Date&quot;: a secret date at Keyaki Mall<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.271–274<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Goes alone to Keyaki Mall before the island exam to try a &quot;mock date&quot; with Ayanokōji — arriving separately and messaging each other while browsing the stores.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;Phew, I&#x27;m kind of nervous.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;This is cute~&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s almost as if he stepped out of a manga…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.273<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;He really is simple-minded.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Playful and affectionate — enjoys the secret text-message date, teases his &quot;terrible taste&quot; in a skull strap, and wants to date him &quot;openly and proudly&quot; as soon as possible; touched that he silently left the kitten strap she liked at her door.<span class=\"pg\">p.271–274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her boyfriend; they hold a secret mock date via messages, and he later leaves the kitten phone strap at her door.<span class=\"pg\">p.271–274<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y3v1-p209-1\">← Before: Karuizawa finds Horikita; sharing her painful past<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-amikura-mako-y3v1-p275-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka amikura-mako","q":"amikura mako  ever since that time  amikura s warning about ichinose at the gym after the survival exam  amikura and ichinose join him  after akiyama calls ichinose away over paperwork  amikura speaks to him alone   honami chan s really changed  huh  it s like  unimaginable when you think about how she was like a few months ago   i m telling you this because  i don t want you to make honami chan sad or hurt her   it s tough for honami chan  falling for a guy who has a girlfriend   you can t just abandon her as a friend  it s not a bad thing  understands ichinose well and watches over her   recounts the misdirected message incident that sparked rumors about ayanokoji  and asks him plainly not to hurt her  knowing she sees him as someone special  her best friend  recounts how the girls helped her through the message rumor and asks ayanokoji to protect her feelings  gym buddy  warns him not to hurt ichinose  sees he is unflustered by the blunt request","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-amikura-mako-y3v1-p275-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/amikura-mako.html#sc-amikura-mako-y3v1-p275-1\">&quot;Ever Since That Time…&quot;: Amikura&#x27;s warning about Ichinose<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.275–283<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/amikura-mako.html\">Amikura Mako<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the gym after the survival exam, Amikura and Ichinose join him; after Akiyama calls Ichinose away over paperwork, Amikura speaks to him alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amikura Mako<\/b> &quot;Honami-chan&#x27;s really changed, huh? It&#x27;s like, unimaginable when you think about how she was like a few months ago…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amikura Mako<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m telling you this because… I don&#x27;t want you to make Honami-chan sad or hurt her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.281<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amikura Mako<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s tough for Honami-chan, falling for a guy who has a girlfriend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.281<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You can&#x27;t just abandon her as a friend. It&#x27;s not a bad thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.282<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Understands Ichinose well and watches over her — recounts the misdirected-message incident that sparked rumors about Ayanokōji, and asks him plainly not to hurt her, knowing she sees him as someone special.<span class=\"pg\">p.275–283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Her best friend; recounts how the girls helped her through the message rumor and asks Ayanokōji to protect her feelings.<span class=\"pg\">p.275–282<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gym buddy; warns him not to hurt Ichinose; sees he is unflustered by the blunt request.<span class=\"pg\">p.275–283<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"}];
